export const ASK_CORPUS = "# GUIDE: Billing SOP (the office: work orders, invoices, payments)\n\n## [billing:job] Chapter 01 · Your job — You own the money side\nOperations is the studio manager's. Billing is yours: work orders, invoices, payments, money owed. Click Next and each part of the screen lights up. Or click any part of the picture.\n### Where you'll live\n- Everything is in the left rail: This is the rail as you see it. These are your stops.\n- Dashboard: Your morning read: Flo's lines, your duties, the money at a glance.\n- Billing: Click it to open its four pages. The word itself never takes you anywhere.\n- Billing Hub: Every work order and invoice, sorted by what it is waiting for. This is where you work.\n- Petty Cash · SRS · Client AP Protocols: Month-end cash, referral payouts, and how each label wants its invoices sent.\n- Daily Ops: Last night, studio by studio. Yours: the red WO not submitted badges.\n- Calendar: Where sessions are booked. Clicking one opens the same work order the hub opens.\n- Training: This manual lives here, with the app guide and its version history.\n### The one rule\nPRSFlo owns the workflow and the documents. QuickBooks owns the money. \"Where is this invoice, and what is it waiting for?\" is a PRSFlo question. \"How much did we make in July?\" is a QuickBooks question.\n\n## [billing:flow] Chapter 02 · A session, start to finish — A session, start to finish\nOne work order, followed from booking to paid. This is the Billing client's path. COD's shorter path is chapter 08.\n### One row, ten stops\n- The same row, ten times: This is one work order as the hub shows it at each stage. The badge says where it is. The button, when there is one, is your next move.\n- 1 · Booked: Every session gets a work order automatically. Until its first day it waits in Not started.\n- 2 · The session runs: The runner works the same work order from their phone and presses Submit each night.\n- 3 · Needs review — yours: A night is in. Open it, check it against what really happened, tap Review ✓ on each day, then Complete WO.\n- 4 · Needs invoice — yours: Make the invoice in QuickBooks. Drag the PDF onto the row.\n- 5 · Needs approval — the owner's: Nothing for you to press. An owner reads the package and approves.\n- 6 · Not approved: The owner sent it back with a note. Fix the work order, re-issue the invoice, drop the corrected PDF on the row.\n- 7 · Ready to send: Approved and the PO is in. Download, email it, then Mark sent the same day.\n- 8 · …or Awaiting PO: Approved, but no PO number yet. Chase the label. Add PO when it arrives. No second approval needed.\n- 9 · Sent: Age counts the days since Mark sent. At 31 it is overdue. Mark paid the day the money lands.\n- 10 · Paid: Done.\n\n## [billing:wo] Chapter 03 · The work order — The work order\nOne document per session. The calendar card, the runner's phone, the hub row and the client's PDF are all this one page.\n### Part by part\n- Words on the left, numbers on the right: Who and what kind on the left. Days, rentals, payments and totals on the right. Below it: one day, opened.\n- Cancel · Complete WO · Save: Save stores and closes. Cancel closes without saving, no question asked. Most typing is only on your screen until you Save.\n- Complete WO: \"I checked this and it is right.\" It saves everything first, payments included, then moves the work order to Needs invoice. It will not complete while a day is missing its times, and a TBD day counts as missing. Press it again on a completed work order to Reopen it: the row drops to In progress with a Reopened tag until you complete it again.\n- The WO number: Automatic. The invoice number sits under it once it is typed.\n- ⟲ HISTORY: Who changed what, and when. It does not record payments, rentals, or the hub's Mark sent and Mark paid.\n- Status: Confirmed, Tentative, Cancelled and Lockout are sessions. Tour, Tech, Open Hrs and Tenant are calendar blocks with no billing.\n- COD or Label/Billing: The big one for you. It decides which side of the hub this work order lives on, and whether the 3% card fee applies.\n- The client card: Who the session is for: label, artist, A&R and their admin. On file means the client has a profile. A typed name alone reads Not on file.\n- Invoice # and PO #: Type the PO, or switch on Not req'd. Without one of them the package cannot be sent.\n- Studio Time: one card per day: The only place the schedule and staffing live. Click a card to open that day.\n- Submitted · Not submitted: Amber: the runner turned that night in, with name and time. Red: the night passed and nobody did.\n- Review ✓: Your check on one day. The small chip on the day card reads Review ✓, then green ✓ Reviewed. It locks the day so the runner can no longer change it. If nobody submitted that night, it submits it in your name.\n- Each day has its own status: Confirmed, Tentative or Cancelled. A cancelled day stays on the work order and bills nothing.\n- Adding days: + Add studio time asks for the dates and the room. + Seed adds a long run in one go and saves at once, so press Save first.\n- Rentals: Charge fills in as Qty × Rate. You can type over it.\n- Payments: On a Billing client it says invoiced, nothing to collect at the desk. Taking a COD payment is chapter 08. Each saved line shows the date it was recorded, in small grey text after the memo.\n- Discount: % or $, with a reason. It comes off studio time and engineering only. This is how a kill fee is done.\n- Totals: Every figure is worked out from the rows above, never typed. If a number looks wrong, read the rows.\n- Food budget: The Food budget pill turns it on. The bubble opens the receipts. The client is billed receipts plus a 45% service fee.\n- Notes: Booking Notes and Needs Attention are internal. Session Notes is the one the client sees.\n- A day, opened: Click a day card and this opens.\n- Start and End: The booked times. This is what bills. TBD means \"not decided yet\", on purpose.\n- Client actually here: Arrived, Left, or No show. A record only. Billed stays as booked.\n- The rate: / HR bills the booked hours. / DAY covers a set number of hours (blank means 12), then overtime at the OT rate.\n- Staff: 1ST and 2ND: Engineer or assistant, their hours, their rate. No rate means no charge.\n- The day's own Save: It only keeps the edit on screen. The Save at the top of the work order is what stores it.\n- Remove hold: Only on a Tentative session. Chapter 07 walks through it.\n### These save the moment you touch them\nCancel will not undo: Review ✓, the × that clears a staff line, food receipts, the equipment pills, the SRS tick, days added with + Seed, and Remove hold (which also saves your edits first).\n\n## [billing:hub] Chapter 04 · The Billing hub — The Billing hub\nRail → Billing → Billing Hub. Every work order is one row. The app moves rows between tabs for you.\n### The page\n- Read a row like this: Badge: where it is. Flag: the one thing worth knowing. Button: your next move.\n- Billing · COD · Tenants: The heading is the switch. This chapter is the Billing side.\n- Four figures: Outstanding, Received this month, Waiting on approval, Over 31 days. The last three jump to their tab.\n- Search: Searches everything at once, Billing, COD and Closed: client, artist, invoice #, WO #, PO.\n- The tabs: In progress is where the work is. Not started is future sessions. Awaiting PO and Awaiting payment are your chase lists.\n- In progress is a queue: Top to bottom: Needs review, Needs invoice, Needs approval, Not approved, Ready to send, then sessions still running.\n- The badge: Where the row is.\n- The flag: The one thing worth knowing about it: Never submitted, Changed since invoiced, the owner's note, or Reopened · recheck the invoice, which means someone reopened the work order after its invoice went on. Check the invoice still matches before it is approved.\n- The button: Your next move. No button: open the row, drop a PDF, or it is someone else's turn.\n- Needs review: Click the row. Check each day, tap Review ✓, then Complete WO.\n- Drop invoice here: Drag the QuickBooks PDF onto the row, or click the chip. The row becomes Needs approval.\n- Needs approval: Waiting on an owner. Nothing for you to press.\n- What the owner sees: A strip above the list on every tab: Ready for your approval. Owners only. You will not see it.\n- Not approved: Hover the flag to read the owner's note. Drop the corrected PDF on the row and confirm Replace it. That sends it back to them.\n- Download, then Mark sent: Download builds one PDF: the invoice plus the work order. Email it, then press Mark sent. Aging starts from that press.\n- AP: How this label wants its invoices sent. Chapter 05.\n- ✎ Collection notes: A running log for chasing money. Chapter 05.\n- ⋯: Everything rare: pull it back, remove a wrong invoice, close, delete. Chapter 06.\n- Removed holds: Holds taken off the calendar. Chapter 07.\n### The flags\n- Submitted by …: The runner turned the night in, and when.\n- Never submitted: A past night nobody submitted, and who closed that studio. 2 days means two nights are missing. It outranks every other flag.\n- Submitted by Lori: The runner missed it and the office completed the work order instead.\n- Needs review / in progress: A long session still running, with a night waiting for you. Review each night as it comes in.\n- Reviewed thru …: A long session still running, and you are caught up.\n- Changed since invoiced: The work order's total no longer matches its invoice. Re-issue the invoice and drop the corrected PDF. The flag stays until the owner approves again.\n- Built, not sent: Downloaded two or more days ago and never marked sent. Send it, or mark it.\n### Awaiting PO\n- Approved, no PO: Your chase list for label POs.\n- Add PO: Opens a strip under the row.\n- The PO number: Type it exactly as the label gave it.\n- A re-issued invoice (optional): If QuickBooks re-dated the invoice, choose the new PDF here. It replaces the one on the row.\n- Save & download: Stores the PO and downloads the package. The owner's approval is not disturbed.\n### Awaiting payment · Paid · Closed\n- Age: Days since you pressed Mark sent. Never since the session date. Oldest first.\n- Over 31 days: The balance turns red. Chase it, and write what you learn in ✎.\n- Mark paid: One press, no question. Press it the day the money lands. Pressed by mistake: ⋯ → Undo Mark paid.\n- Closed: Written off or voided, with the reason on the row. Closed COD rows land here too.\n- Reopen: Puts it back where it was. A sent invoice returns to Awaiting payment with its original date. An approval never comes back.\n### Guardrails you will notice\nChange the money after approval and it un-approves. The owner approved a figure, not whatever it becomes. A sent invoice never changes quietly. The only way to restart it is Pull it back, which is the owner's. These leave no line in History: Mark sent, Mark paid and their undos, Pull it back, Close and Reopen. If it matters later, put a line in ✎.\n\n## [billing:send] Chapter 05 · Packages, AP & notes — Packages, AP & notes\nWhat opens when you click a row, how to send it, and where to keep the chase.\n### The package window\n- Click a row with an invoice on it: The package opens. A row with no invoice opens the work order instead.\n- Work order: The live one. You can edit it right here. Use its own Save or Cancel: the window will not close on unsaved changes.\n- Invoice: The PDF you dropped on the row.\n- Previously saved: The exact file that was last built, page for page.\n- As sent: After Mark sent, that tab reads As sent: the file the client received.\n- What the owner sees: Approve, or Don't approve… with a note. You cannot approve. The button is theirs alone.\n- Returned: The owner's note sits at the top. Fix the work order, then drop the corrected invoice on the row.\n### AP: how to send this invoice\n- Opens from the AP chip: Beside the client's name on the row. One card per label.\n- At a glance: Portal or email, PO required or not, how they pay.\n- The steps: Click a step to tick it as you go. Ticks belong to this work order and everyone sees them.\n- Passwords: Never kept in the app. The card only says where to find it.\n### ✎ Collection notes\n- Write it down every time you chase: Who you spoke to, what they said, what happens next.\n- Your initials and the time: Added for you.\n- Edit, never delete: A note can be edited. It cannot be removed.\n- Internal: Never on the work order, the package or the runner app.\n\n## [billing:undo] Chapter 06 · Undo, close, delete — Undo, close, delete\nEverything rare lives behind the ⋯ on a row. What you see there depends on where the row is.\n### The ⋯ on a row\n- Every item, in one picture: A real row only shows the items that apply to it. This shows them all.\n- Open the attached invoice PDF: Just the invoice, in a new tab.\n- Remove the attached invoice: For a PDF that went on the wrong work order. Only before an owner has approved.\n- No PO required: This one can go out without it. Set per work order.\n- Download the package again: Before Mark sent only. Built fresh from the work order as it stands now.\n- Undo Mark sent: Pressed it too soon? The row goes back to Ready to send. The invoice and the approval stay.\n- Undo Mark paid: The row goes back to Awaiting payment with its original sent date.\n- Pull it back — owners only: Removes the invoice, the saved package and the approval, for good. You will not see it. Ask Eli or Adam-Mike when an invoice has to start over.\n- Close this invoice: Write it off or void it.\n- Pick a reason: You must choose one. Other needs a note. The row moves to Closed with the reason showing.\n- Delete this work order: Every day on it and every calendar card. Next.\n### Deleting, and getting it back\n- Type the WO number: Delete removes the whole work order, so it makes you type its number first. To remove one day, delete that day inside the work order.\n- The page's own menu: It opens from the ⋯ at the top right of the hub.\n- Deleted work orders: Everything deleted is kept: what, by whom, when.\n- Recover → Put it back: Restores it exactly as it was.\n- Recovered: It stays in the list, greyed.\n- Generate WO: Downloads a blank form to print. It creates nothing in the app.\n### Good to know\nOnly you, the manager and the owners can delete. The work order itself has no Delete button. A hold has Remove hold instead: next chapter. Gaps in the WO numbers do not mean something was deleted. Numbers are sometimes skipped.\n\n## [billing:holds] Chapter 07 · Holds — Removing a hold\nA hold is a Tentative session. It comes off the calendar from its own work order, one day or all of it.\n### Remove hold\n- Remove hold: Top left of a Tentative work order, beside Cancel. Confirmed sessions never have this button.\n- Nothing is ticked: The window lists every day of the hold. You choose what goes.\n- Tick the days to remove: Only those days come off. The rest stay on the calendar.\n- Every day ticked: It says so in red first. Then the whole hold goes.\n- A greyed day: A confirmed, submitted or reviewed day is not a hold any more. It cannot be ticked.\n- Nothing is lost: Everything removed is kept under Removed holds.\n### The Removed holds tab\n- The last tab: On both Billing and COD.\n- One line per removal: Which hold, which days, who removed it, when.\n- Days or whole hold: 2 days: some days came off. Whole hold: all of it.\n- Recover → Put it back: A whole hold comes back exactly as it was. Removed days go back on their hold as one-day bars until that work order is next saved.\n- Recovered: It stays in the list, greyed, and stops counting.\n### It will say no when\nThe hold has an invoice or a payment on it, or was completed. Delete it from the hub instead. Someone changed the hold while your window was open. Close it and open Remove hold again.\n\n## [billing:cod] Chapter 08 · COD — COD\nPaid at the desk. The only way COD goes wrong is a balance nobody collected.\n### The COD side\n- Click COD: At the top of the hub. The number turns red when any balance is owed.\n- These tabs are switches: More than one can be on. It opens with Balance due and Needs review: your COD morning.\n- Balance due: The session happened and money is still owed. No button: record the payment on the work order and the row moves by itself.\n- Needs review: Paid up. Check the work order, then Complete WO.\n- Needs invoice: Drop the QuickBooks invoice on the row.\n- Needs approval: COD needs an owner's sign-off too. It waits under Paid.\n- Paid: Paid up and approved. Finished.\n### No Mark sent, no Mark paid\nOn COD, paid is worked out from the payments on the work order. It cannot be marked paid when it is not.\n### Taking a payment\n- COLLECT: Two numbers, the same size. Quote the one for how they are paying.\n- Pick the type: Each type shows its amount. Picking one fills the row in for the full balance.\n- Toward balance: The amount before the fee. For a part payment, type it here.\n- The red number: Fee added. This is what you run on the terminal.\n- last 4: Type the card's last four digits, then Save.\n- The red warning: You typed what the terminal charged, so the 3% went on twice. Use $123.00 fixes it in one tap.\n- waive: Takes the fee off that one payment.\n- Card Fees (3%): Credit and debit cards on COD only. Cash, Zelle, Venmo, Wire, ACH, Check and Other carry no fee.\n\n## [billing:other] Chapter 09 · Tenants · SRS · Petty cash — Tenants · SRS · Petty cash\nThree smaller pieces, each with its own screen.\n### Tenants: the rent board\n- Hub → Tenants: Tenants pay rent, not work orders. One row per tenant per rent period.\n- Mark sent: You emailed the rent invoice. Send by is six days before the period starts.\n- Mark paid: On rent it asks how much, and the date received.\n- The amount is the total so far: When the rest comes in, type the running total, not just the second payment.\n- Partial: Some in, some still open. Mark paid again when the rest arrives.\n- In QB: You entered the payment in QuickBooks. That is the last step.\n- Undo: Tap the status word to take back the last step.\n- Late: Red once rent is five days past the start of its period.\n- The ledger: Tap a tenant's name: every period, invoiced, paid, balance.\n- Incidentals: The one tenant with a work order. Month sheet → shows the runner hours to bill. Send it by the 3rd; it reads Late at 31 days unpaid.\n### SRS payouts\n- Owed: Every session with SRS ticked on its work order, oldest first.\n- The fee: A percentage of the room charges, before any discount. Engineering is not included.\n- The %: Grey is the default, 20%. Tap it to change it for that one session.\n- 20 · 15 · 10, or any %: Only that session changes.\n- Mark paid: Asks the date it went out and locks the amount.\n- Undo: Tap the green chip. It asks first.\n### Petty cash\n- One studio, one month: Pick them here.\n- You enter nothing here: Runners record the cash each night and count the box at close.\n- Opening balance · Closing per ledger: Worked out from the ledger. Nobody types them.\n- Nights the box didn't match: By how much, who counted, and their note.\n- Download CSV · Print: For month-end.\n\n## [billing:dash] Chapter 10 · The Dashboard — The Dashboard\nThe morning read. Flo first, then the money, then your list.\n### Top to bottom\n- Flo: A few lines worked out from real records. Read the red ones first. Chapter 11. The small wave button in the bottom-right corner is Flo too: ask it how to do something in the app, in your own words, and it answers from this guide.\n- The money: COD out, WOs need review, Wait on approval, Ready to go out. Click the box to open the hub.\n- Your list: Your duties and your tasks. Red is late. Click the box for the full list; there, tap the words of a long duty to read all of it, and + Add to give yourself a one-off or a recurring one.\n- A duty: Click to tick it. Click again to untick.\n- Missed days add up: One red line counts the days, today included. One tick clears them all.\n- Monthly duties stay until done: Red, counting the days late.\n- A task: A one-off somebody assigned to you. Click it to open it on the Flags tab.\n- Today's sessions: A card per room. Green is confirmed. Amber is a hold, not billable yet. Today's sessions are tomorrow's review queue.\n- Landed & in the air: New confirmed bookings made today, and the holds to check this week.\n- CRM — pipeline: The sales side. Not yours.\n### A pop-up you will meet\n- Last night: a work order was never submitted: Once a day, if a session from last night was not submitted. It will not come back tomorrow.\n- Open →: Click a line to go straight to that work order.\n### The rules your list lives by\nWeekdays only. Daily duties are due Monday to Friday. Never late on the day itself. Late means an earlier day went unfinished. 🔒 items were set by an owner. You cannot edit or remove them.\n\n## [billing:flo] Chapter 11 · Flo — Flo\nThe lines are a mirror, not an inbox. A line goes away when the thing it describes stops being true.\n### The lines\n- Red: something is broken: A session with no work order: open it and it retries. A booking with no room: open it and set the studio.\n- Red: a duty slipped: Missed yesterday, a backlog of three days or more, or a monthly duty past its date. Do it and tick it. A missed-yesterday line stays until tomorrow.\n- Red: COD is owed: Collect the balance and the line goes. You never tick anything.\n- Amber: work orders need review: On a Monday it starts \"Weekend catch-up\".\n- We landed …: New confirmed bookings made today.\n- The last line: It counts duties only. It can say \"All clear\" under a red money line, so read the red lines first.\n- Full briefing →: Flo's written read of last night's notes, the open flags and the week's holds.\n- For you: The part written for the Billing seat. Read it like a colleague's handover note.\n- Re-brief ↻: Asks Flo to write a fresh one now.\n### When Flo and the hub disagree\nThe hub is right. Flo is a summary. Its COD figure looks back 90 days and includes sessions still running tonight.\n\n## [billing:ops] Chapter 12 · Daily Ops & Flags — Daily Ops & Flags\nMostly the studio manager's page. One thing on it is yours, and it is the first stop of your morning.\n### Daily Ops\n- It opens on Yesterday: The arrows step a day back or forward.\n- Four cards, one per studio: All the same size.\n- The dots: Green came in. Amber came in with a problem. Red never came in. These are mostly the manager's.\n- WO not submitted — yours: A session last night that the runner never submitted. Tap the badge to open the work order.\n- Whose it was: The runner who last saved that work order, or whoever filed the closing checklist.\n- ?: Nobody saved it and nobody closed out that studio.\n- Talk to the runner, then tick it: They can still submit it themselves, even the next day.\n- Handled: It turns grey and everyone in the office sees the same tick.\n- Studio tasks: Small jobs for that studio. Whoever ticks one leaves their initials.\n### What happens to the badge\nThe runner submits late: the badge goes away. The office fixes it (Review ✓ or Complete WO): the badge stays on that night as the record. Your tick says it was dealt with.\n### Flags\n- The second title: Same page. A flag is anything that needs doing.\n- Add a flag…: One line saying what needs doing.\n- Facility · Gear: These go to Tech.\n- Clients & billing · Office: These go to Admin, which includes you.\n- Mine · I assigned: What is assigned to you by name, and every flag you added.\n- Done: On an Admin flag, one tap marks it done.\n- 72 hours: The only alarm. An open flag older than that shows its age in red.\n\n## [billing:rhythm] Chapter 13 · The rhythm — The rhythm\nThe whole job, by when it comes around.\n### Rhythm\n- Every morning: Dashboard: Flo's red lines, then Your list.; Daily Ops: every WO not submitted badge chased and ticked.; Hub, In progress: clear Needs review.; Needs invoice: QuickBooks invoice made and dropped on the row.; COD: Balance due is empty, or you know why not.\n- Through the day: Ready to send: Download, email, Mark sent the same day.; Not approved: fix, re-drop, Replace it.; Mark paid the day money lands.; A line in ✎ every time you chase someone.\n- Every week: Awaiting payment, oldest first. Chase everything over 31 days.; Awaiting PO: chase each label.\n- The 1st: SRS: pay what is in Owed and mark each one paid.\n- Month-end: Petty cash: each studio, read \"Nights the box didn't match\", then Print or Download CSV.\n- Rent: Tenants: send by the date on the row, Mark sent, Mark paid, In QB.\n\n## [billing:help] Chapter 14 · Help & words — Help & words\n### When something looks wrong\n- A number that can't be right: Open the work order and read the rows. Every total is worked out from them.\n- \"Paid\" is more than the total: A card payment where the terminal amount was typed into Toward balance. The red line under the payment offers the fix.\n- A work order has vanished: Hub → page ⋯ → Deleted work orders. For a hold: the Removed holds tab. Then tell Eli.\n- Mark sent or Mark paid by mistake: Row ⋯ → Undo Mark sent, or Undo Mark paid. Nothing else changes.\n- A PDF on the wrong row: That row's ⋯ → Remove the attached invoice. Then drop it where it belongs.\n- A red \"NOT saved\" message: The save failed and the app is saying so. Try again. If it keeps happening, tell Eli.\n- The manual doesn't match the screen: The app changed and the manual didn't. Say so.\n### Words\n- Work order (WO): One session's paperwork. Born with the booking.\n- COD · Billing: Paid at the desk · invoiced after.\n- Submit: The runner turning a night in.\n- Review ✓: Your check on one day. It locks the day. (The chip used to read Mark reviewed.)\n- Complete WO: Your check on the whole work order. Sends it to Needs invoice.\n- Approve: An owner signing off the package. Owners only.\n- Package: The invoice and the work order as one PDF.\n- Pull it back: Strip the invoice and approval and start that row again. Owners only.\n- Close: Write off or void an invoice, with a reason.\n- Hold: A Tentative session.\n- Toward balance: A payment's amount before the 3% card fee.\n- Hours included: The hours a day rate covers before overtime. 12 unless set.\n- No show: The artist never came. A record; the bill does not change.\n- AP: A label's procedure for paying an invoice.\n- SRS: A referral fee on a session's room charges.\n- Duty · Task: A recurring item on Your list · a one-off assigned to you.\n- Flag: Anything that needs doing.\n\n# GUIDE: Runner App Guide (the phone app runners use at night)\n\n## [runner:start] Chapter 01 · Start here — Start here\nTap Next. One part of the screen lights up. You get what to do and why. That is the whole guide.\n### The first screen\n- This is the first screen: You land here after you sign in with your own PIN. (Why: Your PIN is your name. Everything you tick, type or submit is stamped with it.)\n- Check it says your name: Not you? Scroll down, tap Sign out, and sign in with your own PIN. (Why: Work done under someone else’s name is a problem for both of you.)\n- Tap the studio you are standing in: PRS, ARS, ERS or TRS. (Why: It asks every time, on purpose. Runners move between studios, and the wrong studio means the wrong work order and the wrong checklist.)\n- Green = sessions today: How many sessions that studio has today. (Why: So you know what you are walking into before you tap.)\n- Runner notes: Tap a studio, or General, to read its notes right here. (Why: The fastest way to read the last runner’s handoff.)\n- Missed a punch?: Forgot to clock in or out? Report it here. Chapter 13. (Why: A missed punch nobody reports is a wrong timecard.)\n- App guide: That is this guide. Runners manual is greyed out. It is coming soon.\n- Stuck? Ask Flo: The small wave button in the bottom-right corner, here and on your studio page. Ask in your own words: \"how do I submit the work order\", \"the client never showed up\". It answers from this guide. (Why: Faster than scrolling the guide at 2 AM. If it is not in the guide, it says so — then ask the office. It cannot see tonight's sessions, only how the app works.)\n- Report a bug or an idea: App doing something weird? Tell us here. (Why: It goes straight to the office. We cannot fix what we do not hear about.)\n- Sign out when you leave: The last thing you tap, every shift. (Why: Stay signed in and the next person’s work goes under your name. The app also signs you out by itself after 4 hours, and at 8:50 AM.)\n\n## [runner:hub] Chapter 02 · Your studio page — Your studio page\nEverything for your shift is on this one page. Work from the top down.\n### Top to bottom\n- Your home for the shift: From the top: jobs from the office, tonight’s sessions, your checklists, notes.\n- Check the studio and the date: Right studio. Your name. Good. (Why: After midnight the date up here changes. The page does not: it stays on last night until 8:50 AM.)\n- Wrong studio?: Tap ← to pick again. Or tap another studio’s letters.\n- The light bulb: Turns the little ? help bubbles on and off.\n- From the office: Open jobs for this studio. Each one stays here until it is ticked. (Why: This is how the office hands you a job without calling. Read it when you walk in.)\n- Done? Tap the circle: It saves right away, with your initials and the time. Tapped by mistake? Tap again. (Why: The office sees it is done. Nobody has to ask you.)\n- Today’s sessions: One card per session. Tap a card to open its work order. (Why: The work order is how the studio gets paid. It is your #1 job in this app.)\n- The pill on each session: Not submitted = the office has nothing for that session yet. (Why: Never leave with a session of yours still saying Not submitted.)\n- Red COD strip: This client pays at the session, and you take the payment. Chapter 05. (Why: COD means paid at the session. The desk is where that happens, and tonight the desk is you.)\n- Last night’s session, still here: Nobody submitted this one last night. It stays on top for one more day. (Why: Late beats never. If it was yours, open it and submit it now. Tomorrow it is off your page.)\n- Your duties: Checklists and counts. Each tile says where it stands.\n- Memos: A memo is waiting. Tap to read it and sign. A new one also pops up by itself. Chapter 12. (Why: Memos are how the office tells you something that matters. Signing says you read it.)\n- Opening and Closing checklists: Opening if you open. Closing if you close. Chapters 07 and 08.\n- Mic inventory: Greyed out: Coming soon. Nothing to tap here yet.\n- Petty cash: The cash box. Log what goes in and out. Count it at close. Chapter 09.\n- Stock list: Count the supplies. Chapter 10.\n- Notes: The studio’s message board. Chapter 11. (Why: The last runner’s handoff is in here. So is anything the office tagged you in. Read it when you arrive.)\n- A finished night looks like this: Sessions: Submitted. Checklists: Submitted. Petty cash: Counted at close. (Why: Anything still open when you leave, the office has to chase in the morning.)\n\n## [runner:wo] Chapter 03 · The work order — The work order\nOne page per session. You write down what really happened. The office bills from it.\n### The whole page\n- One page per session: Tap a session card and this opens. It is a long page. Scroll. (Why: The office bills the client from this page. Wrong here = wrong invoice.)\n- THE BIG RULE: Nothing you type is saved until you tap Save or Submit. ← and Cancel throw it all away. No warning. (Why: One save for the whole page, so the office never gets half a work order.)\n- Session info is locked: 🔒 Set by the office. You cannot change it. Something wrong? Tell the office in Notes. (Why: Client, dates and price are agreed before the session. They do not change at the desk.)\n- Need the client?: Tap the phone number. It calls them.\n- Bought food for the session?: Only when you see this chip. Tap $ left ›, then + Add expense: the place, the amount with tip, a photo of the receipt. (Why: Food is billed back to the client from these receipts. Each one saves as you go.)\n- Leave the budget number alone: The green amount is what the client agreed to spend. You only add receipts. Leave the service fee % alone too. (Why: They are not locked, but they are the office’s numbers.)\n- Studio time: one card per day: A 3-day session has 3 cards. Find tonight’s. After midnight, tonight is still the date the night started. (Why: Times typed on the wrong day bill the wrong day.)\n- A locked day: 🔒 Approved by the office. You can View it. You cannot change it. (Why: Once the office approves a day, that is the record. Wrong? Tell the office in Notes.)\n- Orange tag = already sent: It shows who submitted that day, and when.\n- Tonight’s card: Tap Edit. That opens tonight. It is the next chapter.\n- Money so far: The app works these out from the office’s rates. Nothing to type here.\n- Rentals: Outside gear rented for this session. One row each. Swipe sideways to see the whole row. (Why: Rentals are billed to the client. A missing row never reaches the bill.)\n- Something was rented tonight?: Tap + Add row. Fill in Item, Supplier, Date(s) used, Qty and Rate. The charge works itself out.\n- Session notes: This prints on the client’s copy. Plain facts about the session only. (Why: Problems do not go here. They go in Needs Attention, which the client never sees.)\n- Payments: This one says Billing: nothing to collect at the desk. If it says COD, you collect. Chapter 05.\n- Totals: The app does the math. They move when End, rentals or payments change. Nothing to type here.\n- Needs Attention / Runner Notes: Something wrong? Broken, missing, damaged, unsafe, a client problem. Write what and where. (Why: This is the only box on the work order that raises a flag for the office. The client never sees it.)\n- Words first. Then a photo.: Tap + Add photo if a picture helps. (Why: The flag is raised from the words, when you tap Save or Submit. A photo with no words raises nothing.)\n- Submit today: The last thing you do on every session. Chapter 06.\n\n## [runner:day] Chapter 04 · Tonight’s times — Tonight’s times\nTap Edit on tonight’s card and this sheet slides up. Fill it in from the top down.\n### The day sheet\n- One night of the session: Three sets of times. Booked. Client really here. Staff.\n- Check the date: It must be the date the night started, even after midnight. The arrows flip to the other days. (Why: Tonight’s times on the wrong day bill the wrong day.)\n- What the client booked: 12h included = the price covers 12 hours. (Why: Anything past that is overtime.)\n- The room: leave it: The office set it. Do not change it. (Why: It is not locked, but the room is part of what the client booked. Wrong room? Tell the office in Notes.)\n- Start and End are the bill: They start as booked. Ran over? Change End to the real time. Left early? Do not touch it. (Why: These are the hours the client pays for. If End stays as booked, the extra time is never billed.)\n- Type it or pick it: Type 1230a or 930p, always with the a or p. Or tap ▾ and pick a half hour. (Why: Without a or p, 930 is read as morning. If the app cannot read it at all, it wipes the box. Look at the box after.)\n- Overtime fills itself in: End is now 12:30 AM. Hours go to 12.5 and the overtime line does the math. (Why: You never type overtime. You only type the real times. On an hourly session there is no overtime line: a later End just bills more hours.)\n- A long-day warning: 14.5 hours? It asks you to double-check AM and PM. It does not stop you. (Why: 12:30 AM and 12:30 PM are twelve billed hours apart.)\n- When was the client really here?: Type when they arrived and when they left. The real clock. (Why: It never changes the bill. It tells the office what happened in the room overnight. They are not here. You are.)\n- You cannot Submit without it: Arrived and Left must both be filled in. (Why: It is the one thing nobody can work out the next morning.)\n- Client never came?: Tap No show instead. (Why: The bill stays as booked. No show just tells the office what happened.)\n- The engineer: Check the name is right. Tap it to fix it. (Why: The engineer’s hours are on the client’s bill, under that name.)\n- 1ST or 2ND: Tap the chip to switch between first engineer and second (assistant).\n- Staff times: match the booked times: They copy Start and End by themselves. Leave them. (Why: Only change them if the office tells you to, like an early setup.)\n- Song title / session info: Type what was worked on. One line. (Why: It prints on the client’s copy. It tells them what the day was for.)\n- Equipment: tap each one: One tap = green = it worked. Each tap saves right away. (Why: It is the record that the room’s gear was fine on your night.)\n- Something not right? Tap it again: Second tap = red. A box opens. Type what was wrong. + Photo adds a picture. (Why: Careful: a red pill is a record, not an alarm. If the office has to act, also write it in Needs Attention.)\n- Billing: Set by the office. You can read it. You cannot change it.\n- This Save only closes the sheet: It keeps your changes on the screen. Cancel undoes this day. (Why: Nothing has reached the office yet.)\n- Now save for real: Save at the top saves and takes you back to your studio page. Session over? Use Submit at the bottom instead. (Why: Tap ← or Cancel instead and everything you just typed is gone.)\n- A locked day looks like this: 🔒 Approved by the office. View only.\n\n## [runner:cod] Chapter 05 · COD: take the payment — COD: take the payment\nCOD = the client pays at the session, and you take it. You need two things: a signature and the money.\n### Signature, then money\n- A COD work order: The same page, plus a signature block.\n- Balance due: Red chip = this client still owes money. (Why: It goes away when the payments you typed cover the balance. Gone does not mean saved.)\n- The terms: Hand the client the phone. They read this. (Why: It says they approve the charges and that payment is due in full at the session.)\n- Print name: Type the client’s name.\n- Signature: They sign in the black box with a finger. Clear starts over. (Why: The signature is the client agreeing to the charges. Without it, a dispute is our word against theirs.)\n- Two numbers. Pick the right one.: Top: cash, Zelle or check. Bottom: card, which is 3% more. (Why: A runner once ran the wrong one, and the studio ate the difference.)\n- Tap “type” and pick how they paid: Every choice shows the amount to take.\n- Toward balance fills itself in: It is the amount before the card fee. Leave it. Do not add the 3% yourself. (Why: The app adds the fee. Add it yourself and it is added twice.)\n- Run the RED number: That is what you type into the card terminal. Here: $422.30. (Why: Red = the balance plus the 3% card fee. Run the smaller number and the studio pays the fee.)\n- waive: Takes the 3% off this payment. Only if the office told you to.\n- Last 4 of the card: Type the last four digits. (Why: So the office can match this payment to the card statement.)\n- Memo: Optional. Anything about this payment the office should know.\n- Red warning?: You typed the card total into Toward balance. Tap Use $410.00. (Why: It warns you. It will not stop you. Read it.)\n- Paying two ways?: Part cash, part card? Tap + Add payment for the second one.\n- Check it says $0.00: Collect is $0.00. Now read the small print: “once saved” and “1 not saved yet”. (Why: The app is telling you: the money is typed in, but it is not on record.)\n- Now Save. This is the one people miss.: The payment is not on record until you tap Save or Submit. (Why: Tap ← now and the app forgets it. You are holding the money and the work order says they still owe.)\n- Saved looks like this: Paid in full. Signature kept. No more “not saved yet”.\n\n## [runner:submit] Chapter 06 · Submit. Every night. — Submit. Every night.\nSession over? Submit before you leave. It is the most important button in the app.\n### The green button\n- The bottom of the work order: Scroll all the way down. The big green button is the last thing on the page.\n- Submit today: Session done, times right? Tap it. It saves everything and sends tonight to the office. (Why: Submitting is the only way the office knows what happened in your room, and what to collect. Unsubmitted work orders get write-ups.)\n- Nothing is invoiced yet: Submit only says “tonight is in”. The office still reviews it. (Why: So do not be scared of the button. Submit.)\n- It stopped you?: Arrived and Left are empty. Tap Go fill it in, then Edit on tonight’s card. Never came? No show. (Why: It is the one thing nobody can work out in the morning.)\n- Orange tag = it is in: After Submit the work order closes. Open it again and tonight carries your name and the time.\n- Made a mistake? Fix it.: Change what was wrong. Tap Update submission. (Why: No penalty. A corrected work order always beats a wrong one.)\n- Forgot last night?: Open it. Fill in Arrived and Left for the night you missed. Then tap the button: it names the day, or just says Submit. (Why: You can submit at any hour. Late is always better than never.)\n- One more time: ← and Cancel throw away everything since your last Save. No warning. (Why: Leaving a work order is never the same as saving it.)\n### What saves by itself, and what does not\nNeeds Save or Submit: times, arrived / left, No show, staff, song title, rentals, payments, the printed name and signature, session notes, the Needs Attention words. Saves by itself: equipment pills, the “what was wrong” note (when you tap out of the box) and its photo, food receipts, Needs Attention photos. Not sure? Tap Save. It saves everything and takes you back to your studio page.\n\n## [runner:open] Chapter 07 · Opening checklist — Opening checklist\nIf you open, this is your list. Do the job, then tap it.\n### Tick, then Submit\n- Opening: The bar and the count show how far along you are.\n- Do the job. Then tap it.: Each tick saves right away. (Why: Only tick what you really did. Your initials go on this list.)\n- Work down the sections: Building, control rooms, kitchen, and on. Top to bottom.\n- Raise a flag: Unusual things only: broken, missing, damaged, unsafe. Say what and where. Add photos. (Why: It becomes a flag the office has to act on. How the shift went goes in Notes, not here.)\n- Your initials: Already filled in. Check they are yours.\n- Save = not finished yet: Takes you back to your studio page without submitting. Your ticks are kept. Come back and finish.\n- Submit opening: List done? Tap it. Ticks alone are not enough. (Why: No Submit = tomorrow the office sees a red “never submitted” on this studio.)\n- Could not finish something?: Submit anyway. Say what and why in Raise a flag. (Why: Submitted with a problem always beats never submitted.)\n- Done: Submit takes you back to your studio page. Open the list again and it says Submitted.\n\n## [runner:close] Chapter 08 · Closing checklist — Closing checklist\nIf you close, this is the last thing you do in the building.\n### The last list of the night\n- Closing: Same as opening. Do it, tap it. Each tick saves. (Why: Closing at 2 AM Friday still belongs to Thursday. The app knows.)\n- Count first, tick second: These two are counts. Tick them only after you counted. (Why: A tick says “I counted”. The petty cash count itself goes in Petty cash. Chapter 09.)\n- The last walk: Opener’s start time, doors, tenants out, alarm, front door, gate. Tick each one as you do it. (Why: A door left unlocked all night is the worst thing a closer can leave behind.)\n- Raise a flag: Same as opening. Unusual things only.\n- Submit closing: The last tap before you walk out. (Why: No Submit = a red “never submitted” in the morning.)\n- Before you close: A session today has not been submitted. The app shows you which one. (Why: Closing is the last moment you are still in the building. It is your last chance to turn it in.)\n- Yours? Tap Submit on that row.: It opens that work order. Submit it. Then come back and close.\n- Not yours?: Session still running, or another runner’s? Tap Not mine — close. (Why: It asks. It does not trap you. The office still sees the open session in the morning, with a name on it.)\n\n## [runner:cash] Chapter 09 · Petty cash — Petty cash\nThe cash box. Write down every dollar in or out. Count the box at close.\n### Log it, count it, close it\n- Opening: What the box should start with: the last count, plus or minus anything logged since. You cannot change it. (Why: Tonight starts where the last count ended. That is how every dollar is tracked.)\n- Box does not match Opening?: Tap Opening to see where the number came from. Do not try to fix it. Count the box and type it into Counted at close. (Why: The difference goes to the office. They would rather know.)\n- Money moved? Tap + Add: Every time cash leaves the box or goes in. (Why: If it is not written down, the box is just “short” and nobody knows why.)\n- What, and how much: Type what it was for. Type the amount.\n- Out or In: It starts on Out: you spent it. Tap it to flip to In: money put into the box. (Why: Almost everything is Out. In is only when someone physically puts money in the box.)\n- The math: Opening + in − out = what should be in the box.\n- Counted at close: Count the real cash. Type the number. It is never filled in for you. (Why: Counting is the whole point. A copied number is not a count.)\n- Green = it matches: The box and the math agree.\n- Short?: Count again. Still short? Type the real number anyway. (Why: That is fine to record. The office would rather know than find out later.)\n- Tap Save: Nothing on this page reaches the office until you do.\n- Closing out: One last look at the numbers.\n- If it is short: It says by how much. Add a note: what you think happened.\n- Tomorrow’s opening: Your count is where tomorrow starts. (Why: Your name goes on this count.)\n- Close out the night: Tap it. Now it is saved.\n- Nothing moved tonight?: Still count the box and type the number in Counted at close. Then tap Counted — no change, and Close out the night. (Why: A quiet night still needs a count. With the box left empty it is recorded as “not counted”.)\n- It asks: “Is this really money going into the box?”: You typed the box total as Cash in. Tap That’s not right. (Why: Cash in is only NEW money put into the box. What was already there is the Opening.)\n- It asks: “This was already recorded”: Money moved again? Tap Add a new entry. Change a saved row only if it was typed wrong. (Why: The office can already see that row. Two entries keep both on the record.)\n- Previous days: The last 14 days. Read only.\n\n## [runner:stock] Chapter 10 · Stock list — Stock list\nCount what is on the shelves. Mark what is running out. That is how it gets bought.\n### Count, mark, save\n- Paramount has two lists: PRS Stock: every night. Office: Wednesdays only.\n- The count at the top: How many items you have counted, and how many are low.\n- Tap a shelf to open it: Fridge, Kitchen, Lounge and so on. Go stand there and count. (Why: It is grouped by place so you count one spot at a time.)\n- Last count: The small number is the last count and its date. (Why: It tells you what is normal. 6 yesterday and 0 today? Count again.)\n- Type how many: Count it. Type the number in Qty.\n- OK or LOW: Running out? Tap OK to flip it to LOW. (Why: LOW is how the office sees what is running out.)\n- Marked LOW: Orange = low. Tap it again to go back to OK.\n- Tap an item’s name to open it: A Notes box, and its last few counts underneath. (Why: A few words help the office: “Half a carton left.”)\n- LOW since…: Dashed = it was low last time. Still low? Tap it once. Restocked? Tap it twice. (Why: Dashed means nobody has checked it tonight.)\n- General notes: Anything about the whole list. This one box saves by itself.\n- Item not on the list?: Tap Missing an item? Tell the office.\n- Save stock list: The office gets nothing until you tap this. (Why: Your typing is kept on this phone, but kept is not sent.)\n- Done: It says Submitted.\n\n## [runner:notes] Chapter 11 · Notes — Notes\nOne message board per studio, plus General for everyone. Read it when you arrive. Write your handoff before you leave.\n### Read, then write\n- Everyone here sees this: Every runner at this studio. And the office.\n- Studio or General: PRS = this studio only. General = every studio. (Why: Handoffs go in the studio tab. They are filed with this studio’s night.)\n- Read first: The last runner’s handoff is here. Read it when you walk in. (Why: It is how you find out what is already going on.)\n- New since you looked: Everything under the orange line is new.\n- Orange bar = it is for you: Someone tagged you.\n- A task for you: A tag plus a time. You tick it on your studio page, under From the office. Not here.\n- Opener, Floater or Closer: Tap what you are tonight before you post. (Why: So the next person knows which shift wrote it.)\n- Type your note: Short and plain. What happened, and where.\n- Add a photo: Tap 📷. Up to 4. (Why: A photo beats a paragraph.)\n- Tag someone: Tap @ and pick a name. (Why: A tag points the note at one person. They see “for you”.)\n- Tag + time = a task: Tag one person and type a time, like 9am. It becomes a task for them. (Why: It lands on their studio page with a tick box. Studio tab only, not General.)\n- Send: Tap it. Posted.\n- Fix your own note: Tap ✎ on a note you wrote. You cannot delete a note. (Why: Notes are a record. Write them like one.)\n\n## [runner:memos] Chapter 12 · Memos — Memos\nMessages from management that you have to read.\n### Read it, sign it\n- Your memos: Every memo you have been sent. Each one says where it stands on the right. (Why: Memos are how the office tells you something that matters.)\n- Unread: Tap it to open it. A new memo also pops up by itself when you open your studio page.\n- Read it. All of it.: It is short on purpose.\n- I’ve read this: Check the initials are yours.\n- Sign & continue: Tap it. Done. (Why: Your initials say “I read this and I know it.”)\n- I’ll read it later: Really cannot right now? On the pop-up, this puts it off. It comes back the next time you open the app. (Why: Putting it off starts a 48-hour clock.)\n- Sign by…: You put it off. The list shows the day it must be signed by.\n- Needs your signature: The 48 hours are up. The app will not let you go on until you sign.\n- Signed: Done. It stays in the list so you can read it again.\n- Read: Some memos only need reading. No signature: you tap Got it.\n\n## [runner:punch] Chapter 13 · Missed a punch — Missed a punch\nForgot to clock in, clock out, or punch a meal? Report it the same day. It takes 30 seconds.\n### Thirty seconds\n- Check the name: It files under the name shown. Not you? Sign out first. (Why: It goes straight to the manager queue under that name.)\n- Which shift: The day the punch belongs to. After midnight, your shift started yesterday: tap Yesterday. (Why: This page goes by the calendar. At 1 AM, “Tonight” means the new day.)\n- What was missed: Clock in, Clock out, Meal out or Meal in.\n- The time it should say: Type it like 6:00 PM. With the colon. Always with AM or PM. (Why: Leave off AM or PM and “6:00” is read as 6 in the morning.)\n- Red message?: The app could not read the time. Type it like 6:00 PM.\n- Note: Optional. One line on why.\n- Submit: Tap Submit as your name. (Why: Same-day reports are the good kind. Report it the night it happens.)\n- Sent: It is in the manager queue.\n- Your last 90 days: Clean, 1 miss, 2 misses. Three or more shows in red. (Why: Reporting a miss is right. Not missing is better: clock in before anything else.)\n\n## [runner:rules] Chapter 14 · The rules — The rules\nIf you remember nothing else, remember these.\n### Nine rules\nYour PIN, your name. Never work under someone else’s sign-in. Pick the studio you are standing in. On a work order, nothing is saved until Save or Submit. ← and Cancel lose it. Ran over? Change End. Left early? Leave it. Always fill in Arrived and Left. Or No show. COD: signature, the right number, Save. Submit every session before you leave. Late beats never. Something wrong? Write it in Needs Attention, or Raise a flag. Everything else goes in Notes. Count the box. Type the real number. Even when it is short.\n### If something goes wrong\n- I submitted with a mistake: Open the work order. Fix it. Tap Update submission. No penalty.\n- I forgot to submit last night: It is on top of your studio page until the next morning. Open it, fill in Arrived and Left, submit. Already gone? Tell the office in Notes.\n- The day I need is locked: The office approved it. Tell the office in Notes.\n- The cash box is short: Count again. Type the real number. Add a note.\n- The app asked for my PIN again: Normal. It signs you out after 4 hours, and at 8:50 AM.\n- The app is doing something weird: First screen → Report a bug or an idea.\n- I do not know what to do: Ask the office in Notes. Tag them with @.\n\n# GUIDE: App guide — CRM, Clients, Petty cash, and what each lead status means\n\n## [app:statuses] Lead statuses — what each one means and the rule for it\n- 🔥 HOT (hot): Serious lead — ready to move. Has a date in mind, knows what they want, has a budget, and understands what Paramount offers. Includes regulars who confirm quickly. These leads are close to revenue. Rule: Contact same day, every time. Call AND text if no answer. Log every attempt. A HOT lead untouched for 24 hours is money walking out the door.\n- ☀ WARM (warm): Interested but not ready yet. Genuinely interested but no specific date, hasn't locked in what they want, no set budget. They need nurturing — consistent presence without pressure. Rule: Touch every 2–3 days. Help them get concrete: a date, a budget, a plan. Share availability and what's been recorded here.\n- ❄ COLD (cold): Low engagement — keep them warm. No recent response or went quiet. Don't drop them — cold leads re-engage. Light, periodic outreach keeps Paramount top of mind. Rule: Once a week max. If no response after 3–4 weeks, reassess.\n- ◎ UNCONTACTED (uncontacted): New — no outreach yet. Just came in. They're probably reaching out to other studios right now. Speed of response is everything. Rule: Contact the same business day. Move to HOT, WARM, or COLD after first contact.\n- ✓ BOOKED (booked): Payment received or label approval confirmed. A lead moves to BOOKED once payment is received (COD) or approval is confirmed from the label. Do not mark as Booked until one of these two things has happened.New client If the client hasn't worked with us before, send the registration link first to collect their Instagram, T&Cs, and ID. Once they complete it their client profile is created automatically. Then click Confirm Client Account — they move to Booked. Returning client If the client already has a profile on file, no registration needed. Once payment or label approval is confirmed, click Confirm Client Account — they're marked as Booked instantly. Rule: Payment received or label approval confirmed — that's the trigger. Not a verbal, not a maybe. Once that's in hand, click Confirm Client Account and proceed to standard booking protocols.\n\n## [app:crm] CRM\n- Adding a New Lead (Most important step): The moment an inquiry comes in — phone, email, walk-in, DM, referral — it goes in the CRM immediately. Not later. Right now. Full name always. Phone AND email every single time. Tip: Open the new lead form while you are on the phone, mid-text, or reading the email. Enter it directly — no paper, no notes app, no waiting until later. That middle step is exactly where leads disappear. One less step, zero missed inquiries. Do: Enter the lead the second it comes in; Full name — no first names only; Phone AND email, every time; Note what they want, timeline, and any budget info Don't: Wait until later — leads go cold fast; Leave fields half-filled; Enter just a first name and a number\n- Logging Every Touch (No log = it didn't happen): Every interaction gets logged — calls, texts, emails, in-person. Even \"left voicemail, no answer.\" This is what keeps the team aligned and prevents leads from slipping. Tip: Log right after the interaction. Be specific: what was said, what's next. Do: Log every attempt, even no-response; Include dates, what was discussed, next steps Don't: Skip logging because it felt minor; Write \"called them\" with nothing else\n- Keeping Statuses Current (Needs Action view depends on this): The Needs Action view shows exactly who needs attention — but only if statuses are accurate. Update the moment something changes. Tip: Just off a call and they're ready to book? Change the status before you do anything else. Do: Update status immediately after any shift in intent; Review leads daily — does this status reflect reality? Don't: Leave a booked lead showing as HOT or WARM; Keep dead leads as COLD indefinitely\n- Working the Needs Action View (Start every shift here): The Needs Action view shows exactly who needs attention right now. This is where every shift starts. Uncontacted first, always — escalate to upper management if you can't handle one, then work your Hot leads. Tip: A fresh inquiry sitting uncontacted? That's the most expensive thing in the CRM — contact it same-day or escalate to management. Do: Open Needs Action at the start of every shift; Contact Uncontacted leads same-day, before anything else — escalate to management if you can't; Then clear your Hot leads; Click Contact and log it after every interaction Don't: Let an uncontacted inquiry sit past same-day; Let HOT leads pile up\n- Booking a Lead (What the whole CRM exists for): Lead approves or pays COD — they move to BOOKED. Click Book Client → New Client, generate their registration link, send it same day. Tip: Don't let the link sit. Send immediately. Follow up in 30 minutes if they haven't registered. Do: Send the registration link same day; Let the client fill out their own profile Don't: Delete the CRM record after booking; Mark BOOKED before approval or payment is confirmed\n\n## [app:clients] Clients\n- Reviewing a New Profile (Incomplete = liability): When a new client appears, review it right away. Don't assume it's complete. ID uploaded? T&Cs signed? Phone and email present? Tip: Make this part of your daily routine. No session happens with an incomplete profile. Do: Check ID is uploaded and legible; Confirm T&Cs signed; Verify phone and email are on file Don't: Assume it's complete because they submitted it; Allow sessions if ID is missing\n- Keeping Profiles Updated (Old info causes real problems): Phone numbers and emails change. Every time a client gives updated info, change it in their profile before the conversation ends. Tip: Any time a client gives you new contact info — open their profile and update it on the spot. Do: Update contact info the moment it changes; Note preferences and special requirements Don't: Leave outdated numbers on file; Use personal texts as the main client record\n- Writing Good Notes (Turns one-time clients into regulars): Notes capture the relationship. What do they care about? Usual setup? Who they work with? This is what makes any team member able to make a client feel like a VIP. Tip: \"Prefers Studio A, works with Marcus, R&B, usually needs parking for 3 cars\" — that's what matters. Do: Add notes after every session or significant interaction; Note preferences, quirks, recurring needs, who referred them Don't: Leave notes empty on active clients; Only write notes when something goes wrong\n\n## [app:petty] Petty cash\n- Reading The Opening Balance (You never type this): The opening is worked out for you: the last time anyone counted the box, plus anything logged since that count. Tap it and it shows you the whole trail — which night was counted, who counted it, and what has moved since. It used to be a number you could type, and it was the same figure every day because it came from when the log first started. Tip: If the opening looks wrong, do not try to correct it. There is nothing to correct — it is a record of what happened. Count the box and type your count at close; the difference is what tells the office something is off. Do: Glance at it at the start of your shift; Tap it if the number surprises you; Trust it — it comes from the last real count Don't: Look for a way to edit it; Assume a strange number means the app is broken; Ignore a big surprise without telling anyone\n- Logging A Transaction (As it happens, not later): Every time money leaves the box, it gets an entry: what it was for, and how much. Write it so someone who was not there understands it — \"Coffee run, Studio B\" not \"coffee\". Log it when it happens, not from memory at 2am. Tip: Include the room or the client where it makes sense. At month end the accountant reads these lines and has to work out what the money was for. Do: Log it the moment the money moves; Say what it was for and where; Use Out for money leaving the box Don't: Save them all up for the end of the night; Write one word and move on; Log a purchase you paid for personally — that is an expense claim, not petty cash\n- Cash In — When It Actually Applies (The one people get wrong): Cash IN means someone physically put money into the box. The office topping it up. Change coming back from a purchase. That is it. It does not mean recording what is in the box, and it does not mean balancing anything out. Tip: If you type a cash-in that is close to the opening balance, the app stops and asks whether you really mean it. That prompt exists because this is easy to get wrong — read it rather than tapping through. Do: Use it for a top-up from the office; Use it for change returned from a purchase; Say who put the money in Don't: Enter the balance as a cash-in; Use a cash-in to correct a mistake — tell the office instead; Tap through the warning without reading it\n- Counting At Close (The most important thing you do): Count the box at the end of your shift and type the total into Counted at close. This is what sets tomorrow's opening for the next person. A night nobody counts is a night the chain has to guess at — it still works, but the next real count is what puts it right. Tip: Count after your last transaction, not before. The count is the anchor: anything logged after it is added on top tomorrow, so counting too early makes the next shift start from a wrong number. Do: Count coins as well as notes; Count after everything is logged; Press Save & close out and read the summary Don't: Count at the start of your close-out; Skip it because nothing moved — a no-change night still gets counted; Guess the total\n- When The Box Does Not Match (Tell us — you are not in trouble): Sometimes the count and the ledger disagree. That is normal and the office would much rather know. Recount first, including coins. Then type what is actually in the box and add a note — a receipt you found, something you remember, or plainly that you do not know. Tip: Your note is read by someone who was not in the room. \"Found a $20 receipt with no entry\" is useful. \"Off by a bit\" is not. Do: Recount before recording; Type the real amount, whatever it is; Write a note, even if the note is \"no idea\" Don't: Adjust entries until it balances; Leave the difference unexplained; Sit on it until your next shift\n\n# WHAT'S NEW — staff release notes, newest first (open: /sop → Version History)\n\n## [new:v1.46.3] v1.46.3 — Oct 22, 2026 — Ask Flo on a phone: fixed the sideways scroll, bigger ask bar, green Ask.\nSmall fixes from the first phone test, plus Flo now gives the closest step instead of refusing when the guide covers your situation in different words.\n- The guide chips under an answer are short (“Runner guide · Tonight’s times”) and wrap, so the screen no longer scrolls sideways.\n- The ask bar and the Ask button are bigger on a phone, and Ask is green.\n- If the guide covers what you are asking but not in your words, Flo gives you the closest step and says so.\n- Your questions are private: they are not shown to other staff.\n- When something is not in the guide, Flo says “ask the office” (runners) or “ask a manager” (office) — not “ask Eli”.\n- The top of the sheet (the ribbon, “Flo”, the ×) is bigger on a phone.\nWhat this means for you: Nothing to do.\n\n## [new:v1.46.2] v1.46.2 — Oct 22, 2026 — Runners can Ask Flo too.\nThe same wave button, on the runner app’s first screen and the studio page.\n- Runners tap the wave button bottom right and ask in their own words — “how do I submit the work order”, “the client never showed up”. Answers come from the Runner guide only.\n- It is not on the checklist, stock, petty cash or work order pages, where the Save / Submit bar lives.\n- Anything about money, invoices or approvals gets “that is the office’s side — ask them.”\nWhat this means for you: Office: nothing changes for you. Runners: it is on your first screen; the guide has a step about it.\n\n## [new:v1.46.1] v1.46.1 — Oct 22, 2026 — The Billing guide is caught up with this week.\nNo new features. The step-by-step Billing SOP now describes the app as it is after this week’s changes.\n- The day-card chip is called Review ✓ in the guide, as it is on screen.\n- Complete WO: the guide says it saves everything first (payments included) and that pressing it again reopens the work order to In progress with a Reopened tag.\n- The hub’s flags: the guide now names Reopened · recheck the invoice alongside the others.\n- Your list: how to open the full list, read a long duty, and add your own recurring item.\n- Ask Flo now knows all of the above, because it reads from the same guide.\nWhat this means for you: If you read the Billing guide last week, the Review chip and the Reopened tag are the two things that changed.\n\n## [new:v1.46.0] v1.46.0 — Oct 22, 2026 — Ask Flo: a help button, bottom right, for “how do I…” questions.\nOffice staff only. Tap the small wave button in the bottom-right corner of any page and ask in your own words.\n- Ask things like “how do I take one day off a hold” or “what does the Reopened tag mean”. Flo answers from the staff guides and gives you a chip that opens the guide at the right chapter.\n- If it is not in the guides, Flo says so and tells you to ask Eli. It does not guess.\n- Flo cannot see work orders, clients or payments — it only knows how the app works. “Where is WO-1214” gets pointed at the billing hub search.\n- Every question is kept so the guides can be improved where people get stuck.\nWhat this means for you: Try it when you would otherwise ask a colleague how something works. If an answer is wrong, tell Eli — that is how the guides get fixed.\n\n## [new:v1.45.4] v1.45.4 — Oct 21, 2026 — Fix: the billing hub is back the way it was.\nFor about half an hour this afternoon, invoiced, sent and paid work orders showed under In progress / Needs invoice. Nothing was changed on them; it was a display rule that was too broad.\n- Every work order is back in the bucket it was in before this afternoon. No invoice, payment or approval was touched.\n- From now on only a work order that someone actually presses Reopen on drops to In progress (with the Reopened tag), until it is completed again.\nWhat this means for you: If you saw rows jump this afternoon, they are back. If anything still looks out of place, tell Eli which work order.\n\n## [new:v1.45.3] v1.45.3 — Oct 21, 2026 — The dashboard greets you by your own name, and the day arrows are fast.\nTwo things Lori and Eli noticed on the phone.\n- The dashboard greeting and the Your List header now show your name. Billing and manager staff were being shown another person with the same role.\n- The &lsaquo; &rsaquo; day arrows on the dashboard’s sessions box no longer reload the whole lead list each click, which is what made them take up to ten seconds on a phone. The first load is lighter too.\nWhat this means for you: Nothing to do. If the dashboard ever shows a name that is not yours, tell Eli.\n\n## [new:v1.45.2] v1.45.2 — Oct 21, 2026 — Complete keeps your payment; reopened work orders go back to In progress; photos on shift notes.\nLori’s notes, same day. One of them was a real bug.\n- Complete WO saves everything first, including a payment you just entered. Before, if the payment was the only change, Complete skipped the save and the payment was lost.\n- A reopened work order moves back to In progress in the billing hub, with the Reopened tag on it, until it is completed again. It no longer sits under Needs approval looking finished.\n- Shift notes take photos. “+ Photo” under the two boxes; they stay with your draft and post with the note. Tap one in the log to see it full size.\n- Each saved payment line on a work order now shows the date it was recorded.\n- On the dashboard, a task raised from a work order or checklist now says which studio and session it is about, not just the runner’s note.\nWhat this means for you: If you see a work order drop from Needs approval to In progress, someone reopened it, or an invoice was attached before it was completed. Complete it to send it back up.\n\n## [new:v1.45.1] v1.45.1 — Oct 21, 2026 — Read a long duty; the review chip fits; reopened work orders say so in the billing hub.\nThree small things staff asked for.\n- Your List: tap the words of a duty to read the whole thing; tap again to fold it. The checkbox still marks it done.\n- Work order day cards: the little review chip now says Review ✓ and no longer sits on top of the Confirmed / Tentative / Cancelled pills. It turns green ✓ Reviewed as before.\n- Billing hub: if a work order that already has an invoice is reopened, its row now shows Reopened · recheck the invoice with who reopened it, until it is completed again. Before, the row looked unchanged.\nWhat this means for you: If you see Reopened on a row under Needs approval, open the package and make sure the invoice still matches before approving.\n\n## [new:v1.45.0] v1.45.0 — Oct 19, 2026 — Lakers: a simpler game card, with names that fill themselves in.\nOwners only. Tap a game and the card is now a short sheet: the game at the top, who it went to, who it was offered to, and the two claims.\n- The game card lost its boxes. Game info sits at the top as plain text (tap it if a date or opponent ever needs fixing). Underneath: Went to, Offered, Claimed, Note.\n- Start typing a name and it suggests people who have had tickets before (with how many), then anyone on file as a client, A&R or artist. Pick one or just keep typing — a typed name is fine and never creates a client.\n- Offered is a plain list, one name per line, with an × to remove. No more struck-through chips.\n- The two ticks are now Claimed (on our account) and Transferred (to them), on the card and on the list.\n- The list updates by itself when something changes on another screen.\nWhat this means for you: Nothing to learn. If a name you type matches someone on file, pick them and the company fills in.\n\n## [new:v1.44.2] v1.44.2 — Oct 14, 2026 — Tenant rooms show light blue on the dashboard.\nMBA and Camper now look the same on the dashboard as they do on the calendar.\n- On the dashboard’s Today’s Sessions grid, tenant rooms (MBA, Camper) are now the light blue tenant colour instead of the green used for booked sessions.\n\n## [new:v1.44.1] v1.44.1 — Oct 13, 2026 — Taking the last engineer or assistant off a session clears them from the calendar.\nThe calendar, the TV displays and the dashboard now match the work order when nobody is staffed.\n- If you remove the only engineer or assistant from a session in the work order and save, their initials now disappear from the calendar card too. Before, the old name stayed on the calendar even though the work order said nobody.\n- This was the stale SL on Katie Vinten’s Oct 12 session. Opening that work order and pressing Save clears it.\n\n## [new:v1.44] v1.44 — Oct 13, 2026 — All-Stars: star your top players.\nA star on every lead and client profile, and an All-Stars filter to see just the starred ones.\n- Open a lead or a client. Next to the name there is a ☆ star. Tap it to make them an All-Star (★). Tap again to take it off.\n- Owners, managers, billing and assistant managers can star people. Everyone else still sees who is starred.\n- One star per person. Star a client and every lead for that client is starred too. Star a lead that belongs to a client and the client is starred.\n- Starred people show a small ★ in the lead and client lists.\n- To see only your All-Stars: on All Leads, tap the ★ All-Stars pill (it shows every starred lead, whatever its status). On Clients, tap the ★ All-Stars tab.\n\n## [new:v1.43.11] v1.43.11 — Oct 13, 2026 — Reviewing a day closes it out, the same as a runner submitting it.\nYou no longer have to wait for midnight to finish a work order whose last day never got a runner submission.\n- When the office marks a day Reviewed, that day now counts as done — exactly like a runner hitting Submit.\n- A no-show on the last day: mark it No show, review it, attach the invoice, and the work order shows Invoiced right away (it used to wait until midnight).\n- A session that ends at 3 PM: if the runner has not submitted yet, reviewing the day yourself lets you invoice and finish it now.\n- The WO not submitted badge on Daily Ops still shows when a runner never turned a night in. Reviewing a day does not hide that.\n- On the work order’s day cards, the green Reviewed chip no longer sits on top of Confirmed / Tentative / Cancelled. It has its own line in the top right corner.\n\n## [new:v1.43] v1.43 — Oct 5, 2026 — Daily Ops is one clean page. Runners can submit late. Deleted work orders can be recovered.\nLast night at a glance in four same-size cards, with Flags as a tab beside it. Runners can submit after 8:50 AM. And nothing that gets deleted is gone for good.\n- Daily Ops is four cards, one per studio, all the same size. Duties and their dots are on the left. On the right: any work order that was not submitted, then the tasks for that studio.\n- A red WO not submitted badge shows the room, the client and the initials of the runner who had it. Tap it to open the work order. Tick it once you have followed up with the runner.\n- Flags is now a tab at the top of Daily Ops (Daily Ops | Flags). It is the same page as before, and old links still land on it.\n- Studio tasks live inside each studio card. Whoever ticks one off leaves their initials.\n- Runners can submit a work order at any time, including after 8:50 AM when a session runs late. Last night’s session stays on the runner list until it is submitted. Until then the office still sees it as not submitted.\n- Signing a work order on the phone: the ink now shows up on the dark screen.\n- Billing hub, safer: a PDF dropped on a sent, paid or closed row is refused, and replacing an existing invoice asks first. A file on the wrong row comes off with ⋯ → Remove the attached invoice.\n- Editing a work order inside the package window: it will not let you close or switch tabs with unsaved changes any more.\n- Mark reviewed on a night the runner never submitted now submits it in your name.\n- Cancel on a work order puts a deleted day back exactly as it was.\n- The Billing manual (Training) has been rewritten from scratch to match the app as it is today. The other manuals follow.\n- Approving invoices (owners): when you press Approve or Don’t approve in the package window, the next one waiting opens by itself. When there are none left it closes.\n- Card payments: the Toward balance box is the amount BEFORE the 3% fee. If you type the amount that ran on the card by mistake, a red line now says so and offers the right number in one tap.\n- No show: if the client never came, tap the No show chip beside Arrived and Left on the work order instead of typing times. You can then submit as normal. The bill does not change.\n- Petty cash: runners can see the last 14 days of counts — the opening amount, money in and out, what was counted, and any over or short.\n- Delete is gone from the work order. A session can only be deleted from the Billing hub (the ⋯ on its row), by Eli, Fernando or Lori. Tour, Tech and Open Hours blocks still have their own Delete.\n- Everything deleted is kept. Billing hub → ⋯ at the top right → Deleted work orders shows who deleted what and when, with a Recover button that puts it back exactly as it was.\n- Remove hold (Oct 7): a tentative hold has a Remove hold button at the top left of its work order, beside Cancel. A window lists the days with nothing ticked. Tick the days to take off, or tick them all to remove the whole hold. Confirmed sessions do not have this button.\n- Billing hub has a new Removed holds tab beside Closed. Every removed hold and removed day is listed there with who and when, and a Recover button.\n- The Ready for your approval strip now shows on every Billing hub tab, not only In progress.\n- Undo Mark sent / Undo Mark paid (Oct 8): pressed one by mistake? The ⋯ on that row now has an undo. The invoice and the approval stay as they are. Pull it back is for owners only now.\n- Paid invoices stop counting days: Age on a paid row is how long the client took. Its amount shows dimmed, because nothing is owed.\n- Tenants: the Incidentals line no longer reads Late the moment it appears. Send it by the 3rd; it turns Late at 31 days unpaid.\n- Petty Cash: the studio buttons, Download CSV and Print can be read in dark mode, and the chosen studio is highlighted.\n- The Billing SOP is now a walkthrough (Training → Billing SOP). Every chapter shows the real screen, lights up one part at a time, and explains it in a line or two. Press Next, or click any part of the picture.\n- The Runner App Guide is new (Oct 12; on the runner’s first screen, App guide). It shows the real phone screens, lights up one part at a time, and gives one thing to do and why. Next is under your thumb.\n- Dashboard (Oct 12): the sessions box has little &lsaquo; &rsaquo; arrows to look at other days. Today takes you back.\nWhat this means for you: Billing: start the morning on Daily Ops and tick each WO not submitted badge after you have spoken to the runner. Runners: if a session ran past 8:50 AM, open it and submit as usual. Everyone: to drop a hold, or some days of a hold, use Remove hold on its work order. To remove ONE day from a confirmed session, delete that day inside the work order. Deleting a work order from the Billing hub removes every day on it.\n\n## [new:v1.42] v1.42 — Oct 1, 2026 — Top clients on the Clients tab; Admin is one dropdown.\nA quick look at who booked the most each month, and a tidier rail.\n- The Clients tab now opens with Top clients: COD by client, Label/Billing by label and A&R. Ranked by sessions, with dollars. Use ‹ › to look at other months.\n- Rates and Positions now live under one Admin dropdown on the rail.\nWhat this means for you: Nothing to do — it is information only.\n\n## [new:v1.41] v1.41 — Oct 1, 2026 — SRS has its own page again — Billing → SRS.\nThe SRS list went missing from the menu. It is back under Billing, it now catches every SRS session, and it shows the actual fee.\n- Every session with SRS ticked on its work order shows up on the list by itself.\n- Owed sessions sit at the top with an orange Mark paid. Paid ones drop below with a green Paid · date chip.\n- The fee is worked out for you from the room charges (engineering is not included). Default is 20%.\n- Tap the % on a session to change it for that one session — 10% for a low rate or an extended booking.\n- Mark paid asks the date it went out and locks that amount. Tap the green chip to undo a mistake.\n- Forgot to tick SRS? Open the work order any time and tap SRS → Just this session. It saves right away and lands on the list.\n- The old SRS spreadsheet (Dec 2023 – Jun 2026) is on the list too, under Paid, marked from the log.\nWhat this means for you: On the 1st, open Billing → SRS, pay what is in the Owed section, and mark each one paid.\n\n## [new:v1.39] v1.39 — Sep 23, 2026 — Petty cash now works like a real cash box.\nThe opening balance used to be the same number every day — it was the figure from when the log first started, not last night's close. It now carries forward properly, and the page only shows tonight.\n- Opening balance is carried for you and can no longer be typed. Tap it to see where it came from — for example “carried from Saturday's count of $360.00, less $20.00 logged Sunday”.\n- The list now shows tonight only. It used to show every transaction the studio had ever logged, which is why the totals looked enormous.\n- Never enter the balance as a transaction. Cash in means someone physically put money into the box — a top-up or a refund coming back. If you type a cash-in close to the opening balance, the app will stop and ask.\n- If the number is not what is in the box, do not try to correct it. Count the box, type it into Counted at close, and the difference goes to the office with a note from you.\n- Closing out now shows a summary first — what it opened at, in, out, what should be there, what you counted — and tells you what tomorrow will open at.\n- Changing something you already saved asks first, and offers to add a new entry instead, so both are on the record.\nWhat this means for you: Runners, every night. Managers: the daily-ops petty cash panel was also showing a meaningless closing balance and is now correct.\n\n## [new:v1.38.3] v1.38.3 — Sep 22, 2026 — The billing hub tells you who, and the calendar stops hiding times.\nThree fixes from the floor. The hub now names the runner on a night nobody turned in and the admin who picked it up, the green badge says what to do instead of what already happened, and a squeezed calendar row keeps its hours.\n- Billing hub: the green badge now reads Ready to send instead of Approved. Same rows, same colour — it just tells you the next move. COD still reads Approved, because there is nothing to send.\n- Billing hub: a night no runner submitted now names the runner who closed that studio out — Never submitted · Cris. Once someone fixes the work order and presses Complete WO, the row turns green and reads Completed by (your name).\n- Pressing Complete WO is also what clears that session from the morning pop-up. If the same sessions keep coming back every morning, it is because the work order was never completed.\n- Calendar: when several sessions share one room in a day the cards get short, and they used to drop the times entirely. They now read 6P–1A Melly Mike on one line — the time first, the name shortened if it has to be.\n- Calendar: a booking running several days keeps each day's own start and end times even when it shares the row with another session. It used to show the first day's hours across the whole run, which was simply wrong on every other day.\nWhat this means for you: Office and billing mostly. Everyone who reads the calendar gets the times back.\n\n## [new:v1.38] v1.38 — Sep 21, 2026 — Hiring walks you through it, and Positions live in the app.\nStarting a hire, promotion or separation is now one question at a time, with a plain-English summary before anything is created. Job titles and what they carry are set on Admin → Positions.\n- Dashboard: a room with two sessions in one day now shows both, stacked in the room's card, each in its own colour. It used to show only the first.\n- Hiring: pick what's happening → who → the position and date (or how a separation is ending) → a review that says exactly what the list will contain and when the deadlines fall. Nothing is created until you press Start on the review screen.\n- The position decides the rest: a job that supervises people gets the 2-hour harassment course and the ADP Manager flag on its list; one that doesn't, doesn't. Vacation days and usual hours come from the position too.\n- Admin → Positions: every job title with supervisory yes/no, vacation days, usual hours, who it reports to, and the job description text. Studio Manager's job description is a draft — please read it and mark it Final.\n- Inside a case, the group you should be working is marked NOW.\nWhat this means for you: Managers only.\n\n## [new:v1.37] v1.37 — Sep 21, 2026 — Hiring: start a case for a new hire, a promotion, or a separation and get the checklist for it.\nThe Hiring page in the HR group is live for managers. One case per person, the list already dated, the ADP steps spelled out.\n- Type a name, pick New hire / Promotion / Separation, give one date — the checklist appears with its dates worked out from that date. Orange dates are legal deadlines; red means it's passed.\n- Every ADP step says exactly where to click in Workforce Now, so nobody has to remember it.\n- A separation asks how it's ending first, because that sets when the final check is due. Letting someone go shows a red banner: the check has to exist before the conversation.\n- Tick anything; the app records who ticked it and when. Close the case when it's done — closed cases stay on file.\n- Next: the offer letter and job description get sent and signed from the case itself.\nWhat this means for you: Managers only. Everyone else sees nothing new.\n\n## [new:v1.34] v1.34 — Sep 18, 2026 — Booking from the calendar now builds the client profile properly — and writes the CRM line for you.\nToo many sessions were booked straight on the calendar with a first name and nothing else, so billing, COD and the CRM had nobody to chase.\n- Client search on the work order shows who you're matching: type, phone or email, how many sessions they've done and when the last one was. An exact name match is marked \"on file\".\n- New client is a short card, not a one-tap add: first and last name, phone or email required. If it looks like someone already on file, it asks — use them, or say it's a different person.\n- The client card says \"On file\" or \"Not on file — just a name\". A bare name gets a \"Put on file\" button that opens the card pre-filled.\n- A confirmed session can't be saved without a client on file. Tentative holds still save with just a name.\n- A confirmed booking made straight on the calendar writes its own Booked line in the CRM — linked to the client and the work order, marked \"from calendar\". Cancel the session and the line goes to DNB.\n- Work orders: each day has its own Confirmed / Tentative / Cancelled pill — one booking can be confirmed Mon–Wed and tentative Thu–Fri. The status bar at the top now sets every day at once and reads \"Mixed\" when days differ. The calendar shows each part in its own colour. A cancelled day stays on the work order, struck through, and bills nothing.\n- Work orders: a TBD button beside a day's Start/End for tentative sessions where the times aren't decided yet — tap it, and the day says \"Times TBD\" on the card and the calendar. Typing a time clears it. A confirmed session won't save with a day marked TBD. Staff slots with nobody named now show a TBD chip.\n- Calendar: a multi-day session shows every day's own times and staff inside the bar — a header band with the name and day count, then one cell per day. Days that match the day before are dimmer so a change stands out; a day with nothing set yet says TBD.\nWhat this means for you: Office. Runners unchanged.\n\n## [new:v1.33] v1.33 — Sep 17, 2026 — Closing can't be submitted while a session isn't. The office sees unsubmitted work orders the next morning.\nAn unsubmitted work order means nobody said what happened in the room — and it's the only way the office knows what to collect.\n- Runners: when you tap Submit closing, any session today that hasn't been submitted stops you — the list is right there, each one opens the work order. Submit them, come back, closing goes through. Submitted with a problem always beats never submitted.\n- Office: the first dashboard visit each morning pops up any work order from the last two weeks that was never submitted, with who closed that studio that night. Each row opens the work order.\n- Billing hub: those rows carry a red \"Runner never submitted\" flag so nobody bills a night nobody looked at. Rows that were submitted say who and when — \"Submitted · Hunter 12:14 AM\" — in the same spot.\n- Multi-day sessions: the badge now says \"Needs review / in progress\" while nights are still to come, and a lockout only shows in Needs review when there's actually a night for you to look at — once you've reviewed what's in, it goes back to In progress until the next night lands.\n- Work orders: each day card says who submitted it and when, instead of a coloured dot.\n- Work order day cards fit the phone again — the rate row wraps instead of pushing the sheet off the screen.\nWhat this means for you: Runners at closing. Office in the morning.\n\n## [new:v1.32] v1.32 — Sep 16, 2026 — Memos can email the office. Techs get a tech dashboard. The day's date on a work order is a chip you can actually use.\nA day of fixes from real use: Tom and Sierra's first login, Eli's dashboard vs. a tech's, and the work-order card.\n- Memos: an \"Also email the office\" toggle on every memo sends owners and office admin a newsletter copy with a link to the full page — no sign-in needed. Runners are never emailed.\n- Techs: the dashboard shows the calendar and tech flags — no CRM, no money, no company briefing. Calendars work for techs now (they didn't before).\n- Work orders: the date on each day card is a small chip — tap − or + to move the whole day, tap the date to pick one. Works on the card without opening Edit.\n- Billing hub: COD opens in the same queue order as billing — balance due, then needs review, invoice, approval. Needs-review rows were getting buried.\n- Dashboard: the \"sessions missing a work order\" alarm no longer counts multi-room and multi-date sessions as missing. Data alarms always show, even on a morning full of duty misses.\n- Owner only: a Delete work order in the billing hub's ⋯ menu, with a typed confirmation.\nWhat this means for you: Office. Techs see a smaller app on purpose.\n\n## [new:v1.31.0] v1.31.0 — Sep 15, 2026 — Notes is a room now: tap in from the hub, tag people with @, and a tag plus a time makes a task for them. There's a General channel every studio sees.\nYou asked for Slack. This is the first half — the room, tagging, General, and \"what's new\" when you open the hub. Phone pings are the second half and are coming.\n- Notes has its own page. On the hub, the Notes card shows the last message and how many are new; tap it to go in. Newest messages are at the bottom, like Messages.\n- Two tabs: your studio and General. General is for everyone at every studio — office too.\n- Tag someone: tap @ and pick them, or type @Hunter. Runners and office are both on the list. If you're tagged, the message gets an orange edge and the hub says \"1 for you\".\n- A tag plus a time makes a task. \"@Hunter 3pm set up B for Lainey\" posts the message AND puts \"Set up B for Lainey · 3:00 PM\" on Hunter's hub under From the office. Check it off there. (Only in a studio channel — General has no hub to land on.)\n- \"New since you looked\" marks where you left off.\nWhat this means for you: Runners and office. Tag people instead of hoping they scroll. Start times go in the same message.\n\n## [new:v1.30.0] v1.30.0 — Sep 15, 2026 — Runner app: search the stock list, count the petty cash box at close, and a mic that moved to another studio is not \"missing\".\nFirst batch from the ERS runner report. Thank you — keep them coming.\n- Stock: a search box at the top of the list. Type \"glove\" and every group opens to the hits.\n- Stock: a few items (waters, bagels) open the full keyboard so you can type \"3 Sm / 3 Large\". Everything else keeps the number pad.\n- Petty cash: a \"Counted at close\" box under the closing balance. Count the box, type it, and the line under it tells you if it matches the ledger or is over/short. A mismatch is not a problem to fix on the spot — the office sees it.\n- Mic inventory: a mic from another studio that you tapped HERE on that studio's tab now shows on YOUR tab under \"Also here · from PRS\", and on the other studio's page it shows \"at ERS\" instead of missing. Rule: a mic from another studio — tap it HERE on THAT studio's tab the night it arrives.\n- Closing checklist: the office run is Thursday (from Wednesday night's office count). The line said Wednesday.\n- The ERS stock list was corrected from your notes (teas, gloves, mop heads, dryer sheets, detergent, D batteries added; Earl Grey, Silk milks, Poms, 2450 batteries removed; ice is \"2 bags per room\").\nWhat this means for you: Runners. Count the petty cash box at close and type what you find.\n\n## [new:v1.29.0] v1.29.0 — Sep 14, 2026 — Memos: when the office sends one, it appears the next time you open the app. Read it, sign it.\nCompany updates, app changes, things that keep going wrong — they come as a memo now, not a text you have to find later. It pops up on your landing screen (the dashboard, or the Runner Hub), you read it right there, and you sign it with your initials.\n- A memo pops up the next time you open the app. Read it, tap \"Sign & continue\" — your initials are already filled in. That’s your signature.\n- Busy? Tap \"I’ll read it later\". It comes back next time you open the app. After 48 hours it stops letting you put it off and you have to sign to go on. The screen tells you when.\n- Some memos are just for reading — those have one button, \"Got it\".\n- Every memo you’ve been sent is on your Memos page: on the rail under Operations for the office, a Memos tile on the Runner Hub for runners. Unread ones are counted on the badge.\n- Owners and Fernando can send memos: type one, or drop in a designed page like the work-order one-sheet — it shows inside the memo, no attachment to open. They also see who has signed, who put it off, and who hasn’t opened the app since when.\n- A sent memo can’t be edited — it can be archived and replaced. Your signature always means the words you actually read.\n- Also fixed tonight: a misspelled client name can be corrected right on the work order (the small ✎ next to the name) and it updates everywhere, including the invoice. Searching a label shows the label with its A&R underneath, and picking it fills the A&R’s email and phone. An artist added to an A&R card saves the moment you press + Add. And the wall displays no longer flip to tomorrow at 5 PM.\nWhat this means for you: When a memo pops up, read it. If you truly can’t right now, put it off once — and come back to it from the Memos tile before it comes back on its own.\n\n## [new:v1.28.0] v1.28.0 — Sep 14, 2026 — Both prices on the desk before you pick a payment, an alarm for sessions with no room, and whole-building rates.\nA runner quoted the cash balance, ran that exact amount on the card terminal, and only then picked Credit Card — so the studio ate the 3%. The work order now shows the cash amount and the card amount side by side, same size, before anything is chosen. Two more things off the list: the app now shouts when a session has no room, and a whole-building day is one price instead of five made-up ones.\n- On a work order, the Payments section starts with a COLLECT box: the amount for cash, Zelle or check, and the amount for a card (with the 3% already in it). Both big, both red, both there from the start. Read the client the line that matches how they’re paying.\n- Pick the payment type and the amount fills itself in — the dropdown even shows the number next to each type. If you type your own amount (a partial payment), it stays yours.\n- Under the box, \"Already collected\" shows what’s been paid so far and how much of it was card fees, so an overtime charge next week clearly carries its own 3%.\n- The old \"If paying by card\" line at the bottom of the totals is gone. That small line under a big Balance Due is what caused the mistake.\n- The dashboard’s Flo line now flags any booking with no room, by WO number. A session with no room appears on no calendar, so nobody sees it coming — four slipped through in September before anyone noticed.\n- Whole-building days: on a work order, any day has a \"Blanket rate\" switch (list view, on the day’s first row — or in the day card’s Billing box). Flip it, type the price for the day, and every room on that day gets its fair share of it automatically (bigger rooms take more). Overtime on a whole-building day is a number you type next to the rate — it is not worked out from the clock, because those deals are always custom — and it is shared across the rooms the same way.\n- The client’s invoice shows a whole-building day as one line — \"Paramount — whole building · Studios A, B, C, E, X · $6,670\" — never the per-room split.\n- Day rates with fewer than 12 hours included: the fix from v1.27.0 didn’t reach the moment a work order opens, so overtime could still show against 12 until you touched a time. It now reads the included hours everywhere.\n- Room rates live in the app now — Admin → Rates (the rail’s Admin group, /rates). When you add a room to a work order (Add dates, the Seed panel, or picking a room on a blank row) it arrives at that room’s rate instead of copying whatever the row above had. It never changes a rate that’s already on a row. Owners, managers and billing can edit the rates there.\n- Billing: packages waiting on the client’s PO now have their own tab, Awaiting PO, instead of filling up In progress. In progress is a queue — Needs review at the top, then needs invoice, needs approval, then packages ready to send — with a heading over each group. When there’s more than one page, the page strip stays pinned at the bottom of the screen and tells you how many more are below.\n- The Seed panel takes more than one room at a time: tap the rooms, pick the dates, and (optionally) type a Blanket rate per day and its OT. One press builds every row, one staff line per day, with the blanket shared across the rooms. Five rooms for two days used to be twelve steps.\nWhat this means for you: At the desk: read the COLLECT box, not Balance Due. Cash line for cash/Zelle/check, card line for a card. Then pick the type and the amount is already there.\n\n## [new:v1.27.0] v1.27.0 — Sep 14, 2026 — Four billing mistakes fixed, and cancelled sessions now get invoiced.\nA handful of work orders were charging the wrong amount — some too much, some too little — and none of it looked wrong on screen. All four are fixed. Cancelled sessions also stop disappearing: they come through to Billing like any other session, because we usually still charge a kill fee.\n- Hourly sessions no longer add overtime on top of the hours. If an 8-hour session runs 9, it bills 9 hours — it used to bill 10. Overtime is a DAY-RATE thing only.\n- Day rates no longer assume 12 hours. On the day card there’s now a \"Hours included\" box next to the room rate — leave it blank for a normal lockout, or type 9 for a 9–6 day, or 4 for a short event. Overtime starts after whatever you put there. The OT rate is right next to it now instead of buried at the bottom.\n- The Billing list was showing balances that were slightly too low on any invoice with a card payment — it was leaving out the 3% fee. The work order was right, the list was wrong. Now they match.\n- Cancel a session and it still shows up in Billing for review, invoice and PO. If you’re NOT charging for it, close it in Billing and pick a reason — it no longer just vanishes.\n- Work orders have a Discount line now, for kill fees. Type 50 and % for half, or a dollar amount, plus a short reason that prints on the invoice. It doesn’t fill itself in — sometimes a cancellation gets billed in full.\n- Closing an invoice now asks why, from a list (written off, voided, duplicate, billing error, settled), plus a box for a note. The note shows on the row so the next person knows what happened.\n- Adding days to a session is one button. \"+ Add studio time\" asks for the first day, last day and the room, so you can add a whole week at once. Sessions in more than one room now draw one clean bar per room on the calendar instead of a separate block for every single day.\n- Booking from a client profile has been removed — it was creating sessions with no room, which then showed up on no calendar at all. Start Booking on a lead now stays greyed out until the lead has a room, a date and a rate, and tells you which one is missing.\n\n## [new:v1.26.0] v1.26.0 — Sep 8, 2026 — Every label's invoice instructions are now in the app, on the invoice.\nYou approve an invoice for Atlantic. Now what — portal or email? Do they need a PO first? There's an AP button on the row that tells you, in steps, for that exact label. 26 label procedures are loaded, taken from the AP structure sheet.\n- On a Billing row, next to the client name, there's a small AP button. Press it and a panel slides in from the right: the steps for sending that label's invoice, whether a PO is required, the portal or the AP email address, and how they pay. It's also in the ⋯ menu, and on the client's profile.\n- The steps are tickable and everyone sees the same ticks. If you get pulled away halfway through a Warner submission, the next person sees exactly where you stopped and who stopped there. Nothing is blocked by them — they're a place to keep count, not a gate.\n- Billing → Client AP Protocols is the new page holding all of them, grouped by major label with their sub-labels underneath, then the independents. Billing and managers can edit any procedure, and link a client to one right there.\n- Passwords are NOT in the app, on purpose. The card tells you which portal and which login email; the password stays in the locked note. Those portals can change where our money gets sent, so they don't belong in a database that gets backed up every night.\n- Wire and ACH added as payment types, everywhere payments are recorded.\n- Work orders that run in more than one room now say the venue with the room — \"PRS A\", \"ARS B\" — because every building has a Studio A.\nWhat this means for you: When an invoice is ready to go out, press AP on the row before you send. If a label's instructions are wrong or out of date, fix them yourself in Billing → Client AP Protocols — no need to ask anyone.\n\n## [new:v1.25.1] v1.25.1 — Sep 7, 2026 — Light mode grew up, and the wall calendars got readable from across the room.\nLight mode is now a proper mirror of the dark theme rather than a washed-out version of it — including the Dashboard, which used to stay dark no matter what. And the studio TVs finally read properly from the far side of a live room.\n- Light mode redone site-wide: a near-white page with the grey boxes slightly darker than the background, so panels sit INTO the page instead of floating on it. The Dashboard follows your theme now.\n- The TV wall calendars: everything is bold. The panels don't all have our font, and without it the names were rendering thin — unreadable from across a room.\n- The TV calendars scroll so TODAY sits in the middle of the screen, with about three weeks behind it and three ahead. No more staring at a month of empty future.\n- A multi-day session now shows a full card on every day it runs, not a thin strip. Only lockouts keep the strip.\n- The wall calendars update within about five seconds of a booking change again.\n- Billing: any live invoice can now be closed with a reason. Some duplicate rows were stuck in AR with no way out.\n- The Owner's Page — a big-print one-pager of the day for the owner.\n- Flo's briefing opens itself once a day, and her headline points jump you to the right place.\nWhat this means for you: If you use the studio TVs, they should now be readable standing at the door, and today should be in the middle of the screen. If a TV looks frozen, check the clock in its top-right corner.\n\n## [new:v1.25.0] v1.25.0 — Sep 7, 2026 — Flo is real now — she reads the notes and writes your morning briefing.\nEvery morning at 8:50, Flo reads last night's shift notes, the runner channel, the open flags, this week's holds, and what's still unticked — and writes the day's briefing herself. Not canned text: she actually reads what you all wrote.\n- Under Flo's statement on the Dashboard there's now \"Full briefing →\". Open it: a shared read of the night for everyone, then a \"For you\" section — YOUR outstanding items only. Nobody sees anyone else's section except the owners.\n- Owners, Fernando and Billing also get \"Brief me now →\" — press it anytime and Flo re-reads everything on the spot (takes about ten seconds).\n- Flo speaks in plain facts. She never invents numbers — the live counters on the dashboard stay the math; Flo reads the words.\n- Booking safety: if you start a booking for someone who already has a session on those dates, the app now warns you before creating a second one — and can take you to the existing session instead. (This is how five Lonzo Ball work orders happened. It can't anymore.)\n- Holds fixed: a hold that already started still shows in \"Holds to check\", and the list no longer cuts off at six.\nWhat this means for you: Read Flo first thing — the shared part is the night in thirty seconds, and \"For you\" is your own catch-up list. If the app warns you a session already exists, click Cancel and check the calendar before creating another.\n\n## [new:v1.24.0] v1.24.0 — Sep 2026 — PRSFlo went dark — and your whole day now lives on one page.\nThe biggest visual change since launch. The app has a new high-contrast look (near-black with bright text), and the Dashboard and My Day pages became ONE page. Everything you used to check in two places is now in one.\n- The Dashboard is your whole day now: Flo's briefing up top (bigger — read it, it knows things), then Today's Sessions, Your List (your duties, tasks and approvals in one list), who we landed today and what's on hold, the CRM pipeline, and where billing is at.\n- My Day is gone as a separate page — everything it held moved to the Dashboard. Old bookmarks just take you home.\n- Shift Notes got its own page in the menu (under Operations). Same composer, same log, more room — plus a Runner Notes tab so all the building's notes are in one place.\n- The whole app is darker and higher-contrast — easier to read, especially at night. Corners are less rounded everywhere too.\n- The Billing hub speaks one colour language now: grey = nothing to do yet, ORANGE = needs review, BLUE = waiting on approval, green = done, red = money owed. The COD page works exactly like the Billing page too — same badges, same buttons, plus a Not started tab and an \"Add a PO number\" option in the ⋯ menu.\n- Billing pages hold still while you work: rows no longer shuffle or leak between page 1 and page 2 every time you press a button.\n- The billing seat is called \"Billing\" everywhere now (tabs, assign menu, briefings) — assign billing tasks to \"Billing\" until the seat is filled.\n- New web inquiries on the Dashboard glow BLUE now, not red — red means a problem, and a new lead is good news.\n- Nothing about how you DO things changed: duties tick the same, notes post the same, everything saves the same.\nWhat this means for you: One page to start your day instead of two. Open PRSFlo, read Flo's briefing, and everything red is what needs you. If something looks unfamiliar the first morning, it's the same information wearing new clothes — and if something looks WRONG, use the DEV feedback board.\n\n## [new:v1.23.0] v1.23.0 — Sep 5, 2026 — Lead pages get a \"Log Activity\" box — notes that stamp themselves with your initials and the time.\nUntil now the only way to get something into a lead's activity history was the Contact button, so updates ended up in the Notes box with no date and no name on them. Now there's a proper place for them.\n- Every lead has a new \"Log Activity\" box, right under Notes. Type what happened — a call, a rate you quoted, what the client said — and press Log. It lands in the Activity list with your initials and the exact time, automatically. You never type the date or your initials again.\n- The Activity list now starts open on every lead, so the whole history is visible the moment you open the lead — no more clicking the little arrow.\n- The regular Notes box is unchanged. Keep using it for the standing facts: who the person is, what the booking needs. Log Activity is for things that HAPPEN: conversations, rate updates, promises made.\n- Activity is live — if a teammate logs a note on a lead you have open, it appears without a refresh.\nWhat this means for you: Two boxes, two jobs. Notes = who they are and what they need (edit it any time). Log Activity = what happened and when (each entry is stamped and permanent). Stop writing dated updates into Notes — log them instead, and the history builds itself.\n\n## [new:v1.22.0] v1.22.0 — Sep 3, 2026 — Billing gets the COD-style color badges, one button per row, and a fast lane for POs that arrive after approval.\nThe billing list is easier to read at a glance and the buttons only ever say the next real thing to do. Plus a new home for future sessions so they stop crowding the working list.\n- Every billing row now wears a big colored badge on the left, just like COD: In progress, Needs review, Needs invoice, Needs approval, Awaiting PO, Approved, Not approved, Sent, Paid. The little Reviewed → Invoiced → Approved dots are gone — the badge says it all in one word.\n- The button on a row is only ever one of four real actions: Add PO, Download, Mark sent, Mark paid. Attaching an invoice is now just dragging the PDF onto the row (or clicking where it says \"Drop invoice here\"). Approving happens in the \"Ready for your approval\" strip at the top, same as before.\n- A PO that arrives AFTER approval no longer means a trip through the work order. The row's button says \"Add PO\" — press it, type the PO, drop the re-issued invoice from QuickBooks, and Save & download. Then Mark sent, exactly as if the PO had been there all along. No re-approval needed — nothing about the money changed.\n- If the label doesn't need a PO at all, that's in the row's ⋯ menu now: \"No PO required\".\n- If an owner pressed \"Don't approve\" on a package, fixing it is simpler: correct the work order, then drop the corrected invoice on the row — that automatically sends it back for approval. No extra button to remember.\n- Future sessions have their own tab: NOT STARTED. They used to pile up at the top of In progress; now In progress only holds work that has actually begun. The new tab lists what's coming, soonest first.\n- Column headers sort: click Balance to see the biggest first, Age for the oldest, click again to flip, and a third click puts it back in date order. When the list is in date order, small day headers group the sessions like the CRM does.\n- Lists show 15 rows per page now, everywhere in billing.\n- Behind the scenes, two important fixes: editing a work order after approval now ALWAYS sends it back for approval, even if a new invoice is attached afterward — and re-downloading a package that was already sent gives you the exact file that went out, never a rebuilt version.\nWhat this means for you: Billing: scan the badge column — amber means it's waiting on someone here, light blue means we're waiting on the label, red means something needs fixing. One button per row is always your next step. When a PO comes in late, do the whole thing from the billing list: Add PO → drop the new invoice → Save & download → Mark sent. Owners: nothing changed for you — approve from the strip or the package window like before.\n\n## [new:v1.21.0] v1.21.0 — Sep 3, 2026 — Rent gets its own place in Billing, the runner app stops guessing which studio you're in, and two \"it wiped my work\" bugs are gone.\nA new Tenants section for the monthly rooms, a long-overdue fix for the checkboxes that appeared to clear themselves, and a round of small repairs from things people reported this week.\n- Billing has a third section: TENANTS. Every monthly room is listed by building — who's in it, the rent, and whether this month has been sent, paid, or entered in QuickBooks. One button per row, always the next step, with an undo arrow if you tap the wrong one. Anything unpaid past the 5th turns red.\n- Mustard's runner hours are worked out for you. Open Tenants → the incidentals line → Month sheet, and you get every day laid out: his runner hours, the Encore A sessions that overlapped, and the split between full-rate and half-rate hours. The total at the bottom is what goes on the invoice. No more spreadsheet.\n- A day where Encore A ran but nobody typed Mustard's runner hours shows as a dashed empty row — so a forgotten day looks forgotten instead of looking like zero.\n- Monthly lockouts no longer nag for start and end times. Mustard is the exception where the runner fills those in live each day, so his work order stays quiet instead of showing thirty red errors.\n- When you set up a monthly lockout there's now a Staff choice: No staff (most tenants — it's just rent) or Assistant (Mustard). No more empty staff lines on thirty days.\n- You can no longer save a work order as CONFIRMED unless every day has a start and an end time. Tentative saves freely — so hold it as Tentative until the times are settled. This is here because a confirmed session with no times lands on the runner to guess.\n- My Day: the bug where navigating away appeared to clear all your checkboxes is fixed. Nothing was ever actually lost — the screen was repainting itself blank after a hiccup loading. It now keeps what's on screen.\n- Runners: mic inventory submitted by someone else now shows up on your phone without closing and reopening the app several times.\n- Runners: the app always opens on the studio picker now. It used to jump you straight into whichever studio you opened last, which is wrong when you move between buildings — pick where you actually are.\n- Runners: Missed a punch, App guide, Runners manual and Report a bug or an idea have moved to that first screen, since none of them belong to one studio. Runner notes are there too — tap a studio to read or post.\n- Runners: petty cash has a \"Counted — no change\" button. If you counted the box and it matched, tap that and you're done — the office sees it was counted instead of showing it as never done.\n- Runners: mic inventory is greyed out for about a week while we finish it. Nothing is broken — it's coming back.\n- Work orders: a receipt photo now shows as a little thumbnail right on the expense line, so you can see at a glance which ones have a picture.\n- Work orders: the session status buttons (Confirmed, Tentative, Lockout…) all fit on one line again — Lockout was hiding off the edge.\nWhat this means for you: Billing: the Tenants tab is the new home for rent — mark each month sent, paid and in QuickBooks as it happens, and use the Mustard month sheet instead of the spreadsheet. Office: expect a stop if you try to confirm a session with missing times — keep it Tentative until you have them. Runners: the app opens on the studio list every time now, and mic inventory is greyed out for a week.\n\n## [new:v1.20.0] v1.20.0 — Sep 1, 2026 — Work orders remember every change, runner notes become one running channel, and invoices line up for approval on their own.\nThree things the old paper-and-Dropbox days did well are back, app-shaped: the folder of invoices waiting for a green light, the original work order you could always read under the pen marks, and the Slack channel where runners just talked.\n- Work orders have a History button (the ⟲ at the top). It shows every change ever made — who changed it, when, and what it was before. Scroll to the bottom and you'll find the ORIGINAL work order exactly as it was created, with a \"Compare to now\" view that highlights what's different.\n- Invoices that are ready for an owner's approval now announce themselves: a green count on Billing in the side menu, a banner on the dashboard, and a list at the top of the Billing page where each one can be approved with one tap.\n- COD sessions need an owner's approval too now — a paid, reviewed COD session shows an Approve button until an owner signs it off. Three lights on every row: Reviewed, Invoiced, Approved.\n- Runners: your shift notes are now one running conversation per studio, right on your studio's home page — like the old Slack. Everything anyone has ever posted is there, newest at the top. Type your note, pick your shift (opener / floater / closer), hit Send. You can add photos too.\n- Whatever you type in the notes is kept even if you close the app or walk away mid-sentence — it's waiting when you come back. Photos you've attached are kept the same way.\n- The office can read and post in every studio's notes channel from Daily Ops — office posts show an \"Office\" badge.\n- Runners: submitting your day after midnight works properly now. The app knows a night runs past 12 — your \"Submit today\" button means the night you're working, not the calendar date.\n- Manager notes now file under the night they're about — a note posted at 1 AM after closing shows with that night's notes, not at the top of the next day.\n- Work orders can record when the client ACTUALLY arrived and left — two dashed boxes under each day's times in the day sheet. This never changes what's billed (billed is always what was booked) and never appears on the client's paperwork. It's our internal record.\n- Daily Ops: flags now show WHO raised them, and each studio's nightly card is split into Opener and Closer so you can see who did what at a glance.\n- You can now change the studio on a day directly from the card view's day sheet — same dropdown as the list view.\n- Assistant managers can now attach and view invoices in Billing.\n- Welcome Sam Jurequi, joining as assistant manager. Quinn's open tasks have moved to Sam.\nWhat this means for you: Owners: watch for the green count on Billing — that's your approval queue, including COD now. Runners: your notes moved onto your studio's home page as one channel — no more separate notes screen, and after-midnight submits just work. Everyone on work orders: check History before asking \"who changed this\" — the answer is in the ⟲.\n\n## [new:v1.19.1] v1.19.1 — Aug 31, 2026 — Your notes stop disappearing, approving an invoice no longer waits on a PO, and the calendar finally works on a phone.\nA round of fixes from real use — most of them things people told us were annoying this week.\n- My Day notes: whatever you type is saved as you go. Leave the page, close the app, pick it up on the iPad later — it's still there. Submit still posts it to the log the same as before.\n- Billing: an invoice can be approved without a PO number. Approving means the work order and the invoice are correct, which you know the day the session ends — the PO can take weeks. The invoice just can't be SENT until a PO is added or the work order is marked \"Not req'd\".\n- The billing card is now called \"Billing Ops\" instead of a person's name, and Fernando can open it from the My Day switch alongside his own.\n- Daily Ops: you can now page forward to Today, not just yesterday. Anything not turned in yet shows as \"not yet\" in grey instead of red — the day isn't over, so it isn't late.\n- Daily Ops: Track is greyed out while it's on a long-term lease. It won't clutter the list or show as missing its checklists.\n- Runner app: there's a \"Report a bug or an idea\" box on your studio's hub page. Type it, add a photo if it helps, hit submit — it goes straight to the office. Whatever you type is saved even if you get interrupted.\n- Runner stock: the number keypad opens straight away instead of the letter keyboard.\n- Runner stock: each item shows the previous day's count next to the box, with the date, so you can compare without leaving the page.\n- Runner stock: the list is now grouped by WHERE things are — Kitchen Fridge, Stock Closet, Bagel/Condiment Bin — instead of what they are. You walk the room once. A \"Group by\" switch at the top puts it back to Type if you prefer.\n- Calendar on a phone: the grid shows all eleven rooms at once now. Tap any session for a summary card with an Expand button if you need the full work order.\n- Calendar on a phone: the day view has a month calendar pinned at the top — tap a date to jump, and a green dot marks days that have sessions.\n- Calendar on a phone: everything is properly centred again, instead of sitting against the left edge.\n- Notes: the bullet button actually shows a bullet now, and the B and bullet buttons light up when they're on.\nWhat this means for you: Managers and assistant managers: the notes change is the big one — type freely and only hit Submit when you actually want it in the log. Billing: you can approve invoices that are waiting on a PO, so nothing sits in the queue for weeks; the send button is what waits now. Runners: the stock list will look reorganised — same items, same job, grouped by where they physically live so you can count as you walk.\n\n## [new:v1.19.0] v1.19.0 — Aug 26–31, 2026 — The 2026 calendar is in, your notes stop disappearing, and the app finally knows a night runs past midnight.\nA big week. This year's bookings were imported from the old WordPress calendar, monthly lockout rooms got proper handling, card payments do their own 3% math, and anything you type into notes now survives leaving the page.\n- Your notes never clear out. On My Day, whatever you type in Session notes and Studio notes is saved as you type — switch to the calendar, close the app, pick it up on the iPad later, and it's still sitting there. Submit still works exactly as before: it posts your notes to the log and signs them with your name. Above the boxes it tells you where you stand — \"kept — safe to leave this page\".\n- Runners: your shift note is now one big field that saves itself the whole shift instead of separate posted entries. Nothing is ever lost, even if the app closes on you.\n- Notes can be formatted. Bold, bullet points, and tab to indent — on shift notes and My Day notes both. Bullets start automatically when you begin typing.\n- Runners: a night no longer ends at midnight. The app rolls the day at 8:50 AM, so your sessions, work orders and checklists stay put through midnight instead of changing under you mid-shift. Your punches still count by the calendar day — that's payroll and it hasn't changed.\n- Runners: the stock list and mic inventory each have a general notes box for the whole list — for things like \"entered from Ezra's account, office run already done\". Both shifts share it and the office sees it.\n- Runners: the app stops logging you out mid-count. If you're actively typing, your session waits.\n- This year's bookings from the old WordPress calendar are now in PRSFlo. Anything in the past is there to look at only — it can't be edited and doesn't create work orders. Anything from today forward works like a normal booking the first time you open it.\n- Monthly lockout rooms have their own status now. The room shows as occupied and gets a real work order for the rent, but it stays out of daily ops — no checklists, no runner visits, no approvals, because nothing daily happens in there.\n- Work orders: type a flat monthly amount and it spreads across the days of the month exactly, to the cent.\n- Work orders: day rate and hourly rate are locked together — a day is always 10 hours of the hourly rate. Change one and the other follows. Special deals still get typed in by hand.\n- Work orders: card payments handle the 3% themselves. Balance Due shows \"If paying by card (incl. 3%)\" — read that number to the terminal, type what actually got charged, and the math is done. No more adding 3% in your head, and it now catches overtime too.\n- Registration: \"Create profile\" actually sticks. The badge used to come back after a refresh as if you hadn't done it.\n- CRM: leads can be marked Leasing — a stage, not a temperature. Leasing leads stay out of Needs Action because they aren't waiting on a call.\n- iPhone: bigger type on the dashboard room cards, and the calendar shows all the rooms with proper scrolling instead of a squeezed-down version.\n- Stock: Ameraycan and Encore have their own office lists now, and the fridge items live together in one Fridge section — because you walk to one fridge.\nWhat this means for you: Everyone, in different places. Managers and assistant managers: the My Day notes change is the one to notice — stop worrying about losing what you typed, and only hit Submit when you actually want it in the log. Runners: the 8:50 rollover is invisible until the moment it saves you, which is any night you work past midnight. Billing and office: the card 3% and the monthly split change numbers you used to work out by hand — check the first few against your own math, and tell Eli if anything looks off by a cent.\n\n## [new:v1.18.0] v1.18.0 — Aug 25, 2026 — Mic inventory is a sheet now — and your test-pass fixes landed.\nEverything from the runner test pass on Aug 24 is in, and the mic inventory page was rebuilt to work like the paper sheet: a zoomed-out grid where one tap marks a mic HERE.\n- Mic inventory: each studio has its own tab (your studio first, then ARS / ERS / TRK / Floating / Odds), with a counter showing how many you've checked. Tap a mic once to mark it HERE; tap it again to say which room it's in, mark it missing, or clear it.\n- Mic inventory: the search bar stays at the top while you scroll, the list no longer jumps back to the top when you tap, and every mic shows a small note of where it was last seen. A red strip warns about anything that's been missing.\n- Stock: adding a new item works properly now — you can type the full name and remove a row you added by mistake before saving.\n- Stock: the list corrections you asked for are in — cleaning items grouped under Cleaning, the X (check-daily) items are Chobani Sweet Cream Creamer / Mini Half n Half / 2% Milk, Pike Place K-Cups replace French Vanilla, and the bagels read Plain, Everything, Cinnamon.\n- You don't need to type your initials anymore — the app fills them in from your login on the checklist and mic pages.\n- The little \"?\" help tips are solid and readable now instead of see-through.\n- The opening checklist now says the office run is Wednesdays (it said Thursdays; the office stock list has always been a Wednesday job).\nWhat this means for you: Runners most of all. The mic page will look very different — that's the point: it's built to feel like the paper sheet. Nothing changed about what you're checking or how it's saved, and your in-progress counts still survive if you leave the page mid-way. One habit to unlearn: there's no \"Other studio mics\" section anymore — find a stray mic under its own studio's tab.\n\n## [new:v1.17.0] v1.17.0 — Aug 24, 2026 — Stock works like the clipboard, your typing never disappears, and food receipts live on the work order.\nThe stock page was rebuilt around the real Paramount lists, anything you type on runner pages now survives leaving the page, and session food spending gets its own section on the work order.\n- Stock: two big buttons — PRS Stock (nightly) and Office (Wednesdays only; it greys out on other days and pulses DUE TODAY on Wednesday). Items sit in collapsible groups, one line each; tap a name for notes and that item's past checks, so you can compare tonight against previous nights.\n- Stock: quantities can be written the way the paper allowed — \"0.5\", \"✓\", whatever the count actually is. The bagels are separate lines per flavor now.\n- If you type something on stock, petty cash or mics and leave the page or lose signal, your typing is still there when you come back. It only clears once a save goes through.\n- Work order: a food/expense section — fill in date, place and amount for each run and photograph the receipts right from the session card. They save instantly and print into the invoice package for billing.\n- Work order: Complete now flips to Reopen, so an accidental Complete can be undone (it asks first). And the red \"Balance due\" only shows on COD sessions — red means collect at the desk.\n- Shift notes are dead simple now: type, submit, done. The log keeps everything in order and you can edit your own posts.\nWhat this means for you: Runners: the stock page is a different shape but the job is identical — count what's there, mark what's low, save. The office list only unlocks on Wednesdays. Your typing surviving a mis-tap is automatic; nothing for you to do.\n\n## [new:v1.16.2] v1.16.2 — Aug 22, 2026 — The iPhone home-screen icon works now.\nIf you added PRSFlo to an iPhone home screen and got a grey tile with a letter \"P\" instead of the logo, that is fixed.\n- Adding PRSFlo (or the Runner app) to an iPhone home screen now shows the proper ribbon icon.\n- If you already have a letter-\"P\" tile on your phone: remove it, open the site in Safari, and Add to Home Screen again.\nWhat this means for you: Nothing in the app itself changed — this was a security setting on our hosting quietly blocking the way iPhones fetch icons. Android and desktop were never affected.\n\n## [new:v1.16.1] v1.16.1 — Aug 22, 2026 — A new look for the PRSFlo mark — the ribbon.\nThe wave logo is now one solid sea-green ribbon instead of three faint grey lines, and the app icon on your phone finally matches the app itself.\n- The logo you see on the login screen, the side rail and the welcome splash is now a single solid wave ribbon in sea green — same shape family as before, just filled in and given its colour back.\n- The app icon on your phone's home screen is the same ribbon on a dark square. The Runner app's icon is the same ribbon in orange, so the two apps stay easy to tell apart.\n- The name reads \"PRSFlo\" again — capital F, small l-o — the way it used to.\nWhat this means for you: Nothing changes in how anything works — this is purely the look. One thing to know: if the app is already on your home screen, your phone may keep showing the OLD icon. If it bothers you, remove the app from your home screen and add it again from the browser; it will pick up the new one.\n\n## [new:v1.16.0] v1.16.0 — Aug 20, 2026 — Financials — nine years of the studio's numbers, in one graph.\nEverything Paramount has billed since 2017 now lives in the app, alongside what the app records today. It sits in the Billing hub next to Billing and COD, and only owners can see it.\n- The numbers that used to live only in the \"PRS Daily Numbers\" spreadsheet — 2017 through this month — are now in PRSFlo, and the graph keeps filling in on its own from work orders going forward.\n- One line, and you choose what it shows: the total, or just room, engineering, assistant or rentals on their own.\n- Pick any room, or a whole building, from the dropdown — including the older rooms that are still in the books.\n- Drag the bar underneath to zoom into a stretch of months, or drag the middle to slide along the years.\n- The dashed line is a comparison. Leave it on \"Previous year\" and it always shows the same months a year earlier, or pick a specific year to measure everything against — 2019, say.\n- Hover any month and it tells you that month's figure, the same month a year before, and how it moved from the month before that.\n- Switch to \"Years\" and every year stacks on one Jan-to-December axis, so this July sits directly on top of last July and the one before. Turn individual years on and off underneath.\n- The current month is drawn with a dashed line and a hollow dot because it is not finished yet — and it is compared against the same run of days last year, not the whole month, so a half-finished August does not look like a collapse.\nWhat this means for you: Nothing changes in how you build a work order. This is a reading screen for owners — but it is fed by the work orders everyone fills in, so the rates and staff lines you enter are what it draws.\n\n## [new:v1.15.1] v1.15.1 — Aug 20, 2026 — Launch-night fixes — PIN login works, and building a session now has the rate and the engineer right where you need them.\nEverything here came from actually using the app on launch day. If you tried a PIN earlier and it would not let you in, that is fixed — use the same PIN you were given.\n- PIN login works. If yours was rejected earlier tonight, nothing is wrong with it — the app was checking for a 4-digit PIN while yours is 6. Same PIN, try again.\n- If a login ever fails now, the screen tells you WHY instead of just saying \"something went wrong\".\n- Work order, building a session: the room rate (and the /HR · /DAY switch) now sits right under the room times, and the engineer or assistant line is always there under it with their own rate — no more hunting at the bottom of the page.\n- The engineer/assistant times fill themselves in from the room times, and keep following them if you set the room times afterwards.\n- Every staff line has a small × — use it if you added a second engineer by mistake. On the main line it means \"no staff on this day\", which is rare but there.\n- Each day card now shows the rates behind the total, and says \"rate?\" in orange where one is missing — so an under-billed session is visible at a glance.\n- Equipment pills go all the way around now: not checked → OK → Not OK → back to not checked. If you tapped one by accident before a session, you can clear it.\n- Typing times: Tab now jumps straight from Start to End instead of stopping on the little arrow.\n- When a client sends their registration back, the banner now shows their NAME with a Create profile button right there — you rarely need to open anything.\n- Fixed the New Lead search list showing the form through it.\nWhat this means for you: If your PIN did not work earlier, try it again — it was the app, not your PIN. And when you build a session, everything you need is now on the day itself: times, room rate, who is on it, and their rate.\n\n## [new:v1.15.0] v1.15.0 — Aug 20, 2026 — Launch day — the new PRSFlo is live, you log in with a six-digit PIN, and the app knows who you are.\nThe redesign everyone has been previewing is now THE app. Along with it: a new way to log in, your name shown wherever your work is filed, editable shift notes, and a simpler billing page. Here is what changed for you.\n- You now log in with your own SIX-DIGIT PIN on the number pad — no more typed passwords. Your PIN is handed to you personally; it is yours alone, and everything you do files under your name. If you ever need the old email login, use \"Forgot password\".\n- On the runner tablets, the app greets you by name and shows who is signed in at the top of every screen. If it is not your name, sign out and tap in your own PIN — it takes two seconds.\n- The missed-punch form now says \"Submit as [your name]\" right on the button, so a punch can never be filed under the wrong person.\n- Runner tablets sign themselves out after 4 hours (and every morning at 8:50) so the next person always logs in as themselves.\n- Shift notes can now be EDITED — tap an entry to fix a typo. Fixed entries show a small \"edited\" tag. At 8:50 each morning the night's log submits itself and is sealed; then a fresh log starts. Notes written after midnight now count toward the night they belong to.\n- Billing: the \"Upcoming\" list is gone. Every work order that isn't sent yet lives in \"In progress\", with sessions that haven't started sitting at the bottom wearing a \"Not started\" tag — nothing hides in a separate list anymore.\n- Billing, COD side: the tabs now work like switches — you can turn on Balance due AND In progress at the same time and see both as one list, with a colored tag on each row saying which is which.\n- The guides all moved to TRAINING in the sidebar: the app guide, the Billing SOP and the Studio Manager SOP each have a card there, along with the helpful-hints switch. This guide also got the new look.\n- The work order got day-one polish: it starts at the top of the screen, the buttons are bigger, and you can delete a day card or remove a staff line with the little ×.\n- When you text a client their registration link, it now shows as \"Paramount Client Registration\" from our own web address — not an internal app name.\nWhat this means for you: One habit to build, runners especially: when you take over a tablet, glance at the name on screen. If it isn't you, sign out and PIN in — two seconds, and it keeps everyone's hours, notes and punches filed right.\n\n## [new:v1.14.0] v1.14.0 — Aug 18, 2026 — The work order is laid out in two halves now — who the job is for on the left, what it costs on the right.\nOn a computer, the work order used to be one long page you scrolled top to bottom. It is now two columns side by side: everything about the client and the session on the left, and every number — days, staff, rentals, payments, totals — on the right. Nothing was removed and nothing became read-only; it is the same work order, arranged so you can see the client and the money at the same time. On a phone it is completely unchanged.\n- Two columns on a computer: the client and the notes on the left, all the money on the right. You no longer scroll past the client to get to the total and back again to check who it was for.\n- The top of the page is now a proper letterhead — our name and address on the left, the work order number large on the right with the invoice number and OPEN/COMPLETED under it. The WO number is always visible now.\n- The client card is locked to the top left. For a label job the LABEL is the big name (it is who we bill), with the artist under it and the A&R and the Admin side by side — both with their full email and phone. Email, call and text are now small ✉ ☎ 💬 buttons beside each name.\n- Invoice #, PO # and Food budget sit in one row directly under the client card.\n- The notes now read in order and look different from each other on purpose: Booking notes (internal, orange tag) → Session notes (the client-facing one, plain) → Needs attention.\n- Needs attention is now a single slim strip at the bottom of the left column instead of a big empty box. It opens the moment there is something in it, and \"+ Add\" opens it when you want to write something. Notes and photos work exactly as before.\n- The days list and the rentals list now scroll separately, so a long session no longer squashes the rentals and a long rentals list no longer pushes the days off screen.\n- If there is more below in either list, the app tells you — the bottom fades and a \"↓ 2 more days\" tag appears, and it disappears when you reach the end. No more wondering whether you have seen every day.\n- The running total under the days list is itemized now: Studio, then a line for each engineer and assistant by name, then any overtime, then the big total. It was a small chip before.\n- Payments and the totals stay pinned at the bottom right — they never scroll away while you work.\n- On a session card, the song / session notes for that day now have their own space in the middle of the card instead of trailing off the bottom line.\n- Anywhere the app has to name a room on its own it now says the venue too — PRS B, ARS A, TRS North — never just \"B\".\nWhat this means for you: Everything you could type into before, you can still type into — this changed where things sit, not what they do. The printed/emailed PDF is completely unaffected. Two things to know: the days list now shows about three or four days at a time and you scroll for the rest (watch for the \"↓ more\" tag at the bottom), and in the table view you may need to scroll sideways a little to reach the last columns. On a phone nothing has changed at all.\n\n## [new:v1.13.0] v1.13.0 — Aug 17, 2026 — Manuals, helpful hints, a Settings home — and the app now says \"day\", never \"night\".\nGetting ready for launch: runners get an in-app guide to the app, small helpful hints appear across every page (you can turn them off), rarely-used buttons moved into Settings at the bottom of the menu, and Engineers got its own page.\n- Runners now have an App Guide on their studio page — short chapters on how to use every screen. The Runners Manual slot (the job itself) stays \"coming soon\".\n- Helpful hints: small blue ? markers now appear next to things worth knowing — tap one for a tip. They are ON for everyone to start. To turn them off: Settings at the bottom of the left menu (or the 💡 on the runner page).\n- Settings: light/dark mode, hints, the SOP and Sign Out now live under one ⚙ Settings button at the bottom of the left menu. Your everyday pages stay where they were.\n- Engineers has its own page under Operations — the roster with add, edit and deactivate. The old Admin page is out of the menu; everything it held has moved or is being rebuilt.\n- Daily Ops: the \"Needs you\" list now shows 10 at a time (with page arrows) so studio tasks never scroll out of view, and the studio cards lead with the DATE — use the ‹ › arrows or swipe to look back at any previous day. That replaces the old ops log.\n- Wording: the app now says \"day\" and \"yesterday\" instead of \"night\" and \"last night\" everywhere — the studios run 24/7 and the words now match.\n- Every runner is getting their own personal login (email + password) — what you check off and submit is recorded under your name.\n- A session can no longer be saved without picking a VENUE for each studio day (the studio dropdown, e.g. \"Paramount · A\"). Without one, the session could exist but never show on the calendar.\n- Editing a day from the card view on a desktop now opens a proper centered window instead of a phone-style sheet.\nWhat this means for you: If the little blue ? circles bother you, Settings → Hints turns them off in one tap and the app remembers. And if you are used to finding light/dark mode at the bottom of the menu — it is still there, just inside Settings now.\n\n## [new:v1.12.0] v1.12.0 — Aug 16, 2026 — The runner day sheet grew up, overtime figures itself out, and the open work order is live in both directions.\nThe day sheet was redesigned around big, honest time entry; overtime is now computed from the clock instead of typed; and while a work order is open, changes made by the office and the runner appear on each other's screens live.\n- The day sheet now pairs the studio's times with each staffer's times in matching blocks — staff times follow the studio's until you change them. Big time boxes you can type into (\"930p\" works) or pick from a dropdown that opens AT the time already shown.\n- Overtime is automatic for runners: if the session ran past what was booked (or past 12 hours on a lockout), the OT line appears on its own, computed from the clock. Nobody types OT math any more, so it cannot disagree with the times or double-bill.\n- If a day runs past 14 hours the app asks \"really?\" — it warns but never blocks. Long sessions happen; typos get caught.\n- Swipe (or use ‹ ›) to flip between the days of a session. Days the office already approved open in view-only.\n- While a work order is open, office edits land on the runner's screen live and vice versa — your own unsaved edits always win on your screen.\n- The status pill on the runner's session card now answers the runner's question: Not submitted / Submitted / Approved.\n- Dates on the work order read like dates — \"August 17th, 2026\".\nWhat this means for you: For runners: stop calculating overtime — enter the real start and end times and the OT line takes care of itself. For the office: a rate fix you make while a runner has the work order open reaches their phone immediately; no more \"close and reopen\".\n\n## [new:v1.11.0] v1.11.0 — Aug 16, 2026 — The runner work order and the office work order are now the same work order.\nRunners and the office now look at the identical document — the runner just sees the office-only parts locked. Plus a cards view for phones, and the app greets by time of day because the studios never close.\n- The runner work order is the same screen the office uses, with the office's parts locked: the client block says \"Set by the office\", rates show as plain text, and approved days are untouchable. Everything a runner actually does — times, staff, equipment, song titles, payments, signature — stays fully live.\n- A new cards view shows one card per day; tap it to open the day sheet with just the things you type. Phones start in cards for short sessions; the office desktop keeps the full table. A toggle flips either.\n- Submit sends your day to the office — and you can keep fixing it afterwards. The button just becomes \"Update submission\". The only thing that locks a day is the office approving it. The rule: you can always fix your day until the office approves it.\n- Calling the A&R is always allowed — the phone number is a tap-to-call button even inside the locked block.\n- The app now greets by the clock — \"this morning\", \"today\", \"tonight\" — because a 7am shift is not \"tonight\".\nWhat this means for you: Runners: submitting is not final — if something changes at the end of the session, fix it and press Update submission. Correct beats frozen. Office: a runner's save now updates the calendar cards too, same as yours.\n\n## [new:v1.10.0] v1.10.0 — Aug 14, 2026 — The runner app becomes a real product, managers get a morning Daily Ops page — and security is now actually on.\nStudio tasks from the office, missed-punch reports, shift notes replacing the Slack post, one-tap studio memory — and a new Daily Ops page that answers \"did yesterday go right?\" in one look.\n- The office can leave tasks for a studio — they appear at the top of the runner's page, because \"anything waiting for me?\" is the first question of a shift. Tasks belong to a studio and shift, never a person.\n- Missed a punch? Report it in the app the same day — clock in, clock out or meal, the shift date and the real time. Managers get a Punches page to approve and enter them in ADP. This is the written confirmation the law requires, and it protects the runner.\n- Shift notes replace the end-of-shift Slack post: write entries through the shift, each stamped with who and when, photos welcome, handoffs supported. Entries are permanent — records, not drafts.\n- The app remembers your studio — no more picking it every time. The pills at the top switch studios; ← forgets.\n- New Daily Ops page for managers: everything from yesterday that needs a decision on the left (worst first — and a checklist that NEVER came in is now the loudest thing on it), all four studios at a glance on the right. When the list is empty it says \"Yesterday is done.\"\n- Security tightened across the whole app — every table is now properly locked to the roles that should see it.\nWhat this means for you: Runners: the punch report only works from your own login — and do it the same day. Managers: Daily Ops is your morning door now; the flags, the missing checklists and the missing mics all come to you there.\n\n## [new:v1.9.1] v1.9.1 — Aug 13, 2026 — The work order PDF now looks like the work order — and a few things that quietly did nothing now work.\nWhen you download a work order it is finally the real thing: the same sections, the same columns, the same totals you see on screen, in black and white. There is also a blank one you can generate and fill in. And several buttons that looked available but did nothing have been fixed.\n- Download a work order and it now matches what is on your screen — studio time with every day and who worked it, rentals, notes, payments and the totals. Before, it was a generic invoice that did not look like the work order at all.\n- Song names and session details typed into Session Info now print IN FULL. The line grows as tall as it needs to. On screen it still shortens to keep the window manageable, but nothing is hidden on the paper copy.\n- Booking Notes and Needs Attention / Runner Notes NEVER appear on the PDF. They are internal, and they are now locked out of it rather than just left off it.\n- New: \"Generate WO\" in the ⋯ menu at the top of Billing. It makes an empty work order you can type into and print, or print and fill in by hand — for the rare time you need a paper one. It does not create a session and nothing appears on the calendar. If the session is real, still enter it properly.\n- When you download a package, the invoice comes first and the work order behind it — that is the order a client expects to open it in.\n- The studio column now says PRS A or TRS North instead of just \"A\". Every venue has a Studio A, so on paper the letter alone meant nothing.\n- Approve was stuck on any invoice that had been edited after the invoice was attached — you could press it and nothing happened, forever. Fixed. Approving now signs off on the numbers as they stand right now.\n- Complete WO now actually saves and closes. Before it only marked the work order complete and left you sitting there, so you had to press Close afterwards.\n- Editing Session Notes, Print Name, Needs Attention or the signature now counts as a change, so Complete WO stops being greyed out.\n- Equipment Condition: you can now tick OK or ✗ on EVERY day, not just the first one. If a session ran longer than first booked, the extra days were unclickable.\n- The buttons and the red warning bar on the work order have moved to the TOP, next to the title. On a long work order a bar at the bottom is a bar you have to go looking for.\n- The work order will now warn you if an ENGINEER has hours but no rate — that line would bill nothing. It will also warn you if the same person is on two lines for the same day, which charges them twice. Assistants are not included, because they are never rated.\n- Studio Time now groups each day together with the engineer or assistant who worked it, in one shaded block, instead of stripes.\n- Equipment Condition has moved INTO the day. Each day now has an Equipment line with Speakers, Microphone and Console on it. Tap once for OK (green), tap again for Not OK (red) — and Not OK opens a box to say what was wrong and add a photo. The old separate equipment grid is gone.\n- Tapping never puts an item back to blank. Blank means nobody has checked it yet, which is worth knowing, so it cannot be undone by accident.\n- The buttons at the top of a work order are now just Cancel, Complete WO and Save — and they stay on screen while you scroll down the work order.\n- PO: instead of a separate Yes/No, the PO box itself has a small \"Not req'd\" button inside it. Press it when a client does not use POs. Food budget is now just an amount box — leave it empty if there is none.\n- On the Billing page, Billing and COD are now both in the big title at the top, each with a count. If COD has money that was never collected, its number turns red. It is there so COD does not get forgotten.\nWhat this means for you: Two habits worth keeping. First: if you see the red bar at the top of a work order, read it — it is telling you something will bill wrong, not that you did something wrong. Second: the blank \"Generate WO\" form is for handing someone a piece of paper. If a real, paid session ends up on one, it still has to be entered as a proper session afterwards or it never gets invoiced.\n\n## [new:v1.9.0] v1.9.0 — Aug 12, 2026 — Billing — one page for every work order and invoice. Dropbox folders are gone.\nEverything that used to live in the Dropbox folders — needs approval, awaiting PO, sent, paid — now happens on one Billing page in the left menu. You do not file anything any more. The page works out where each job is from the work order itself.\n- A Billing page replaces the old WO Hub. It has a Billing / COD switch at the top, because the two work completely differently — billing gets invoiced and chased, COD is already paid and just needs checking.\n- Every line shows three little lights: Reviewed, Invoiced, Approved. Amber is the one it is waiting on. In the morning, the amber \"Reviewed\" lines are last night's work orders that nobody has looked at yet.\n- Double-click any line to open it. Before an invoice is attached that opens the work order; after, it opens the whole package so you can see the work order and the invoice together.\n- Drag a QuickBooks invoice PDF straight onto a line to attach it. No uploading, no filing, no remembering which folder.\n- Only Eli and Adam-Mike can approve, and nothing can be approved until it has been reviewed, has an invoice attached, and the PO is sorted.\n- The PO now lives on the work order, next to the invoice number, with a \"PO req'd — Yes / No\" switch beside it. If a client never needs one, set it to No there and the job stops waiting.\n- Download and Mark sent are two separate buttons. Download builds the package; Mark sent is you confirming it actually went to the client. Anything downloaded but not marked sent for two days turns red so a finished package cannot sit forgotten in someone's downloads.\n- Made a mistake? \"Pull it back\" in the ⋯ menu takes it out of Awaiting payment, removes the invoice and the approval, and puts it back at the start so you can redo it properly.\n- Change a work order after it was approved and the approval clears itself — an approval is for a set of numbers, not for the job in general.\n- On the work order: Close & Save is now just Close. If you changed nothing it simply closes; if you did, it asks whether to save or discard. Complete WO saves and closes, and greys out when there is nothing to save.\n- COD sessions have their own side, and Balance due is first — those are the rare ones where money was not collected, and they matter most.\nWhat this means for you: You never file anything again. If a line has no button, nothing is waiting on you — double-click it to look. If a button is greyed out, the flag beside it says why. The one habit to build: put the PO on the work order, or press No if the client does not use one, because nothing gets approved until that is answered.\n\n## [new:v1.8.0] v1.8.0 — Aug 10, 2026 — My Day — your daily checklist, on the dashboard and its own page\nThe things your role is responsible for every day now live in PRSFlo instead of on paper. There is a short checklist on your dashboard, and a fuller \"My Day\" page in the left menu with your holds, balances and shift notes. Fernando, Aaron and Eli only.\n- A \"My day — duties\" list on your dashboard. Tick things off as you do them.\n- A new My Day page in the left menu, under Dashboard, with more detail — holds, balances, and a place for shift notes that saves itself as you type.\n- A few duties ask for a number when you tick them (timecard exceptions cleared, Ramp transactions, COD accounts). The box appears after you tick.\n- Weekly and monthly jobs only appear on the day they are due, so Friday's work never clutters Monday's list.\n- The Flo box at the top of your dashboard now writes a real summary from all of this, instead of the example text it has been showing.\n- Anything monthly that gets missed — like tenant rent invoices — stays on your list and turns red until it is done, rather than disappearing until next month.\n- Two duties were removed because the app now does them for you: creating work orders (they are made automatically when a session goes on the calendar) and the daily calendar look-ahead.\n- New for billing: a reminder on the 1st of each month to round up SRS bookings for payment.\n- Work orders now need a start and end time on every row before they can be completed. If one is blank you get a message and the row is highlighted. Runners get the same warning but can still save.\nWhat this means for you: Your list is fixed by your role — you cannot add to it, and it resets each morning. Ticking is safe and you can untick. If your list has something on it that is not really your job any more, say so and it can be removed in a couple of minutes. If a work order will not complete, look for the red message above the buttons — it names the row that is missing a time.\n\n## [new:v1.5.1] v1.5.1 — Jul 30, 2026 — Runner work orders open properly on multi-day sessions\nIf a session ran over more than one day, or moved between rooms, tapping it on the runner sometimes said \"Work order not yet created — contact office\" even though the work order existed. That is fixed.\n- Every day of a multi-day session now opens the right work order.\n- Sessions that use two rooms in one day open correctly from either room.\n- On a phone, the top menu no longer sits on top of the work order — you can see the whole thing.\n- The red line under the work order heading is gone. It only ever appeared on Ameraycan sessions and it did not mean anything was wrong.\nWhat this means for you: If you were told \"contact office\" on a session you knew was booked, that was this. Try it again — it should open. If it still does not, that one is worth reporting.\n\n## [new:v1.5.0] v1.5.0 — Jul 29, 2026 — PIN login is switched off — everyone uses email and password\nSomeone on the internet was repeatedly guessing PINs at our login screen. Nobody got in, and no client information was touched. We have turned PIN login off completely while we rebuild it properly.\n- There is no number pad on the login screen any more. This is deliberate — the app is not broken.\n- Sign in with your email address and your password.\n- Everyone was signed out, and everyone has been given a new password.\n- PINs will come back later, longer and tied to your own phone. We will tell you when.\nWhat this means for you: If you open the app and the number pad is missing, that is expected — use your email and password instead. If you cannot get in, text Eli rather than trying repeatedly. Do not share your password with anyone, including other staff; you each have your own now.\n\n## [new:v1.4.3] v1.4.3 — Jul 29, 2026 — DEV tab — feedback plus test checklists\nThe Feedback tab is now called DEV and has sections down the left. Feedback works exactly as before. There is also a Testing section, used when we need someone to check new work.\n- Feedback is unchanged — same form, same board, just one click deeper.\n- Testing holds checklists for new work. It asks for a PIN; a manager will give it to you if you are testing.\n- A checklist opens as a small window you can drag anywhere, so it stays with you while you move around the app.\nWhat this means for you: Nothing changes for day-to-day work. If you are asked to test something, go to DEV → Testing, pick the batch, and work down the list marking each item Works or Broken. Write what you actually saw in the note — that is the part that gets things fixed.\n\n## [new:v1.3.0] v1.3.0 — Jul 29, 2026 — Runner work order is easier to read, and staff are easier to change\nThe Studio Time table on the runner work order got a clean-up, and you can now swap the engineer or assistant on a session without leaving the page.\n- Text is bigger and numbers are brighter — the old size was too small to read on a phone.\n- Date and Studio stay put when you scroll the table sideways, so you never lose track of which day you're looking at.\n- The Studio column is new. Two rooms on the same day used to look like the same booking listed twice.\n- A multi-day work order now opens on today only, with an All days button when a client asks about the whole run.\n- Tap the engineer or assistant initials → Change → pick from the staff list, or type a name that isn't on it.\n- Assistants no longer show a rate — they were never charged on the work order.\n- Session notes now open full screen. They used to open behind the keyboard where you couldn't see them.\n- The studio name is now the big heading on session cards, on the runner hub and on the dashboard.\nWhat this means for you: Changing an engineer or assistant on the runner applies to that day only — you're recording your own shift, so you can't accidentally change days you're not working. Changing a whole run is done in the office with Batch Edit. If a session runs in two different rooms on one day, you'll now see both rooms clearly — that's not a duplicate.\n\n## [new:v1.2.1] v1.2.1 — Jul 29, 2026 — Runner login works — one PIN pad for everyone\nThe runner hub is reachable again. There is one login screen for the whole team: type your PIN and the app takes you where you belong.\n- Runners share a single PIN. Typing it goes straight to the runner hub — no dashboard, no extra taps.\n- Everyone else lands on the dashboard exactly as before.\n- Reopening the app when you're already signed in takes you to the right place too, not always the dashboard.\nWhat this means for you: Runners: use the shared PIN on the studio device and you'll go straight to studio select. If you're asked for a PIN and it's rejected, tell a manager — don't keep retrying, the pad locks for 30 seconds after five wrong attempts.\n\n## [new:v1.2.0] v1.2.0 — Jul 28, 2026 — Set the engineer or assistant on the lead\nStaffing is now chosen on the lead itself, and it fills in the Work Order for you. Before this, you picked staff nowhere and then typed the same name onto every single line of the Work Order by hand.\n- The old \"Engineer Needed\" button on a lead is now three buttons — Eng, Asst, and No Staff.\n- Next to it, a name box that lists your actual staff. Engineers show for Eng, assistants for Asst, and anyone marked \"Both\" shows for either.\n- Whatever you pick fills in every line of the Work Order when the session is booked.\n- You can type a name that isn't on the list — a new hire or a freelancer — without adding them in Admin first.\nWhat this means for you: Picking a name is optional. If you know a session needs an engineer but not who yet, choose Eng and leave the name blank — the Work Order still reads 1ST so the rates are right, and you fill the name in later. New sessions default to Asst, since that's the normal case. Switching between Eng and Asst clears the name on purpose, because that person was in the other pool.\n\n## [new:v1.1.1] v1.1.1 — Jul 28, 2026 — Start Booking is back on the lead\nThe Start Booking button has returned to the lead detail, next to the registration button. It takes you straight into the Work Order with the lead's details already filled in.\n- Start Booking opens the Work Order with the dates, times, rate, studio and client already populated from the lead.\n- If the lead has no client profile yet, you'll confirm the client first, then land in the Work Order.\n- The lead flips to Booked when you save the session — not when you press the button.\nWhat this means for you: You can open a Work Order to check a rate or availability and back out without closing the lead. It stays in your pipeline where it belongs. Marking a lead Booked from the temperature pill is still a separate action — use it when a deal is closed but the dates aren't settled yet.\n\n## [new:v1.1.0] v1.1.0 — Jul 28, 2026 — Registrations database, shared tasks, and lead date ranges\nA batch of CRM improvements — the biggest being that completed registrations are now permanently searchable instead of disappearing after review.\n- New Registrations tab in the CRM. Every client who has ever completed a registration, searchable by name, email or phone, filterable by date, 25 to a page.\n- Copy Address button on a registration record. One click copies the full billing address, ready to paste — no more copying it a cell at a time.\n- Assistant manager tasks are shared. Quinn and Isaac now both see anything assigned to Asst Mgr. Same for Sierra and Tom on Tech.\n- Leads can hold a date range. If a client asks for a week, record the whole week — the Work Order opens on the full range instead of a single day.\n- New web inquiries flash in the CRM lead list, not just on the dashboard.\n- The Incomplete tab is gone from Needs Action. Those leads were already showing under Uncontacted, Hot or Warm, so the count was double-counting them.\n- Fixing a client's name updates it everywhere — every booking on the calendar and every lead attached to them.\n- Labels can be created with just a company name — no A&R contact required.\nWhat this means for you: The registration review banner now sits at the top of the CRM on every tab, so you'll see returned registrations while you're working leads instead of only on the Clients tab. Your Needs Action count will look lower than before — that's the double-counting being removed, not leads going missing.\n\n## [new:v1.0.0] v1.0.0 — Jul 2026 — CRM live to the team\nThe starting point — the CRM in daily use: leads, statuses and timers, the Needs Action view, client profiles, registrations, tasks and flags.\n- Everything covered by the CRM, Clients, Tasks and Flags guides in this handbook.\nWhat this means for you: If you're new, start with the CRM tab on the left and work through it. Everything after this point is listed above as a change to it."
export const ASK_CORPUS_RUNNER = "# GUIDE: Runner App Guide (the phone app runners use at night)\n\n## [runner:start] Chapter 01 · Start here — Start here\nTap Next. One part of the screen lights up. You get what to do and why. That is the whole guide.\n### The first screen\n- This is the first screen: You land here after you sign in with your own PIN. (Why: Your PIN is your name. Everything you tick, type or submit is stamped with it.)\n- Check it says your name: Not you? Scroll down, tap Sign out, and sign in with your own PIN. (Why: Work done under someone else’s name is a problem for both of you.)\n- Tap the studio you are standing in: PRS, ARS, ERS or TRS. (Why: It asks every time, on purpose. Runners move between studios, and the wrong studio means the wrong work order and the wrong checklist.)\n- Green = sessions today: How many sessions that studio has today. (Why: So you know what you are walking into before you tap.)\n- Runner notes: Tap a studio, or General, to read its notes right here. (Why: The fastest way to read the last runner’s handoff.)\n- Missed a punch?: Forgot to clock in or out? Report it here. Chapter 13. (Why: A missed punch nobody reports is a wrong timecard.)\n- App guide: That is this guide. Runners manual is greyed out. It is coming soon.\n- Stuck? Ask Flo: The small wave button in the bottom-right corner, here and on your studio page. Ask in your own words: \"how do I submit the work order\", \"the client never showed up\". It answers from this guide. (Why: Faster than scrolling the guide at 2 AM. If it is not in the guide, it says so — then ask the office. It cannot see tonight's sessions, only how the app works.)\n- Report a bug or an idea: App doing something weird? Tell us here. (Why: It goes straight to the office. We cannot fix what we do not hear about.)\n- Sign out when you leave: The last thing you tap, every shift. (Why: Stay signed in and the next person’s work goes under your name. The app also signs you out by itself after 4 hours, and at 8:50 AM.)\n\n## [runner:hub] Chapter 02 · Your studio page — Your studio page\nEverything for your shift is on this one page. Work from the top down.\n### Top to bottom\n- Your home for the shift: From the top: jobs from the office, tonight’s sessions, your checklists, notes.\n- Check the studio and the date: Right studio. Your name. Good. (Why: After midnight the date up here changes. The page does not: it stays on last night until 8:50 AM.)\n- Wrong studio?: Tap ← to pick again. Or tap another studio’s letters.\n- The light bulb: Turns the little ? help bubbles on and off.\n- From the office: Open jobs for this studio. Each one stays here until it is ticked. (Why: This is how the office hands you a job without calling. Read it when you walk in.)\n- Done? Tap the circle: It saves right away, with your initials and the time. Tapped by mistake? Tap again. (Why: The office sees it is done. Nobody has to ask you.)\n- Today’s sessions: One card per session. Tap a card to open its work order. (Why: The work order is how the studio gets paid. It is your #1 job in this app.)\n- The pill on each session: Not submitted = the office has nothing for that session yet. (Why: Never leave with a session of yours still saying Not submitted.)\n- Red COD strip: This client pays at the session, and you take the payment. Chapter 05. (Why: COD means paid at the session. The desk is where that happens, and tonight the desk is you.)\n- Last night’s session, still here: Nobody submitted this one last night. It stays on top for one more day. (Why: Late beats never. If it was yours, open it and submit it now. Tomorrow it is off your page.)\n- Your duties: Checklists and counts. Each tile says where it stands.\n- Memos: A memo is waiting. Tap to read it and sign. A new one also pops up by itself. Chapter 12. (Why: Memos are how the office tells you something that matters. Signing says you read it.)\n- Opening and Closing checklists: Opening if you open. Closing if you close. Chapters 07 and 08.\n- Mic inventory: Greyed out: Coming soon. Nothing to tap here yet.\n- Petty cash: The cash box. Log what goes in and out. Count it at close. Chapter 09.\n- Stock list: Count the supplies. Chapter 10.\n- Notes: The studio’s message board. Chapter 11. (Why: The last runner’s handoff is in here. So is anything the office tagged you in. Read it when you arrive.)\n- A finished night looks like this: Sessions: Submitted. Checklists: Submitted. Petty cash: Counted at close. (Why: Anything still open when you leave, the office has to chase in the morning.)\n\n## [runner:wo] Chapter 03 · The work order — The work order\nOne page per session. You write down what really happened. The office bills from it.\n### The whole page\n- One page per session: Tap a session card and this opens. It is a long page. Scroll. (Why: The office bills the client from this page. Wrong here = wrong invoice.)\n- THE BIG RULE: Nothing you type is saved until you tap Save or Submit. ← and Cancel throw it all away. No warning. (Why: One save for the whole page, so the office never gets half a work order.)\n- Session info is locked: 🔒 Set by the office. You cannot change it. Something wrong? Tell the office in Notes. (Why: Client, dates and price are agreed before the session. They do not change at the desk.)\n- Need the client?: Tap the phone number. It calls them.\n- Bought food for the session?: Only when you see this chip. Tap $ left ›, then + Add expense: the place, the amount with tip, a photo of the receipt. (Why: Food is billed back to the client from these receipts. Each one saves as you go.)\n- Leave the budget number alone: The green amount is what the client agreed to spend. You only add receipts. Leave the service fee % alone too. (Why: They are not locked, but they are the office’s numbers.)\n- Studio time: one card per day: A 3-day session has 3 cards. Find tonight’s. After midnight, tonight is still the date the night started. (Why: Times typed on the wrong day bill the wrong day.)\n- A locked day: 🔒 Approved by the office. You can View it. You cannot change it. (Why: Once the office approves a day, that is the record. Wrong? Tell the office in Notes.)\n- Orange tag = already sent: It shows who submitted that day, and when.\n- Tonight’s card: Tap Edit. That opens tonight. It is the next chapter.\n- Money so far: The app works these out from the office’s rates. Nothing to type here.\n- Rentals: Outside gear rented for this session. One row each. Swipe sideways to see the whole row. (Why: Rentals are billed to the client. A missing row never reaches the bill.)\n- Something was rented tonight?: Tap + Add row. Fill in Item, Supplier, Date(s) used, Qty and Rate. The charge works itself out.\n- Session notes: This prints on the client’s copy. Plain facts about the session only. (Why: Problems do not go here. They go in Needs Attention, which the client never sees.)\n- Payments: This one says Billing: nothing to collect at the desk. If it says COD, you collect. Chapter 05.\n- Totals: The app does the math. They move when End, rentals or payments change. Nothing to type here.\n- Needs Attention / Runner Notes: Something wrong? Broken, missing, damaged, unsafe, a client problem. Write what and where. (Why: This is the only box on the work order that raises a flag for the office. The client never sees it.)\n- Words first. Then a photo.: Tap + Add photo if a picture helps. (Why: The flag is raised from the words, when you tap Save or Submit. A photo with no words raises nothing.)\n- Submit today: The last thing you do on every session. Chapter 06.\n\n## [runner:day] Chapter 04 · Tonight’s times — Tonight’s times\nTap Edit on tonight’s card and this sheet slides up. Fill it in from the top down.\n### The day sheet\n- One night of the session: Three sets of times. Booked. Client really here. Staff.\n- Check the date: It must be the date the night started, even after midnight. The arrows flip to the other days. (Why: Tonight’s times on the wrong day bill the wrong day.)\n- What the client booked: 12h included = the price covers 12 hours. (Why: Anything past that is overtime.)\n- The room: leave it: The office set it. Do not change it. (Why: It is not locked, but the room is part of what the client booked. Wrong room? Tell the office in Notes.)\n- Start and End are the bill: They start as booked. Ran over? Change End to the real time. Left early? Do not touch it. (Why: These are the hours the client pays for. If End stays as booked, the extra time is never billed.)\n- Type it or pick it: Type 1230a or 930p, always with the a or p. Or tap ▾ and pick a half hour. (Why: Without a or p, 930 is read as morning. If the app cannot read it at all, it wipes the box. Look at the box after.)\n- Overtime fills itself in: End is now 12:30 AM. Hours go to 12.5 and the overtime line does the math. (Why: You never type overtime. You only type the real times. On an hourly session there is no overtime line: a later End just bills more hours.)\n- A long-day warning: 14.5 hours? It asks you to double-check AM and PM. It does not stop you. (Why: 12:30 AM and 12:30 PM are twelve billed hours apart.)\n- When was the client really here?: Type when they arrived and when they left. The real clock. (Why: It never changes the bill. It tells the office what happened in the room overnight. They are not here. You are.)\n- You cannot Submit without it: Arrived and Left must both be filled in. (Why: It is the one thing nobody can work out the next morning.)\n- Client never came?: Tap No show instead. (Why: The bill stays as booked. No show just tells the office what happened.)\n- The engineer: Check the name is right. Tap it to fix it. (Why: The engineer’s hours are on the client’s bill, under that name.)\n- 1ST or 2ND: Tap the chip to switch between first engineer and second (assistant).\n- Staff times: match the booked times: They copy Start and End by themselves. Leave them. (Why: Only change them if the office tells you to, like an early setup.)\n- Song title / session info: Type what was worked on. One line. (Why: It prints on the client’s copy. It tells them what the day was for.)\n- Equipment: tap each one: One tap = green = it worked. Each tap saves right away. (Why: It is the record that the room’s gear was fine on your night.)\n- Something not right? Tap it again: Second tap = red. A box opens. Type what was wrong. + Photo adds a picture. (Why: Careful: a red pill is a record, not an alarm. If the office has to act, also write it in Needs Attention.)\n- Billing: Set by the office. You can read it. You cannot change it.\n- This Save only closes the sheet: It keeps your changes on the screen. Cancel undoes this day. (Why: Nothing has reached the office yet.)\n- Now save for real: Save at the top saves and takes you back to your studio page. Session over? Use Submit at the bottom instead. (Why: Tap ← or Cancel instead and everything you just typed is gone.)\n- A locked day looks like this: 🔒 Approved by the office. View only.\n\n## [runner:cod] Chapter 05 · COD: take the payment — COD: take the payment\nCOD = the client pays at the session, and you take it. You need two things: a signature and the money.\n### Signature, then money\n- A COD work order: The same page, plus a signature block.\n- Balance due: Red chip = this client still owes money. (Why: It goes away when the payments you typed cover the balance. Gone does not mean saved.)\n- The terms: Hand the client the phone. They read this. (Why: It says they approve the charges and that payment is due in full at the session.)\n- Print name: Type the client’s name.\n- Signature: They sign in the black box with a finger. Clear starts over. (Why: The signature is the client agreeing to the charges. Without it, a dispute is our word against theirs.)\n- Two numbers. Pick the right one.: Top: cash, Zelle or check. Bottom: card, which is 3% more. (Why: A runner once ran the wrong one, and the studio ate the difference.)\n- Tap “type” and pick how they paid: Every choice shows the amount to take.\n- Toward balance fills itself in: It is the amount before the card fee. Leave it. Do not add the 3% yourself. (Why: The app adds the fee. Add it yourself and it is added twice.)\n- Run the RED number: That is what you type into the card terminal. Here: $422.30. (Why: Red = the balance plus the 3% card fee. Run the smaller number and the studio pays the fee.)\n- waive: Takes the 3% off this payment. Only if the office told you to.\n- Last 4 of the card: Type the last four digits. (Why: So the office can match this payment to the card statement.)\n- Memo: Optional. Anything about this payment the office should know.\n- Red warning?: You typed the card total into Toward balance. Tap Use $410.00. (Why: It warns you. It will not stop you. Read it.)\n- Paying two ways?: Part cash, part card? Tap + Add payment for the second one.\n- Check it says $0.00: Collect is $0.00. Now read the small print: “once saved” and “1 not saved yet”. (Why: The app is telling you: the money is typed in, but it is not on record.)\n- Now Save. This is the one people miss.: The payment is not on record until you tap Save or Submit. (Why: Tap ← now and the app forgets it. You are holding the money and the work order says they still owe.)\n- Saved looks like this: Paid in full. Signature kept. No more “not saved yet”.\n\n## [runner:submit] Chapter 06 · Submit. Every night. — Submit. Every night.\nSession over? Submit before you leave. It is the most important button in the app.\n### The green button\n- The bottom of the work order: Scroll all the way down. The big green button is the last thing on the page.\n- Submit today: Session done, times right? Tap it. It saves everything and sends tonight to the office. (Why: Submitting is the only way the office knows what happened in your room, and what to collect. Unsubmitted work orders get write-ups.)\n- Nothing is invoiced yet: Submit only says “tonight is in”. The office still reviews it. (Why: So do not be scared of the button. Submit.)\n- It stopped you?: Arrived and Left are empty. Tap Go fill it in, then Edit on tonight’s card. Never came? No show. (Why: It is the one thing nobody can work out in the morning.)\n- Orange tag = it is in: After Submit the work order closes. Open it again and tonight carries your name and the time.\n- Made a mistake? Fix it.: Change what was wrong. Tap Update submission. (Why: No penalty. A corrected work order always beats a wrong one.)\n- Forgot last night?: Open it. Fill in Arrived and Left for the night you missed. Then tap the button: it names the day, or just says Submit. (Why: You can submit at any hour. Late is always better than never.)\n- One more time: ← and Cancel throw away everything since your last Save. No warning. (Why: Leaving a work order is never the same as saving it.)\n### What saves by itself, and what does not\nNeeds Save or Submit: times, arrived / left, No show, staff, song title, rentals, payments, the printed name and signature, session notes, the Needs Attention words. Saves by itself: equipment pills, the “what was wrong” note (when you tap out of the box) and its photo, food receipts, Needs Attention photos. Not sure? Tap Save. It saves everything and takes you back to your studio page.\n\n## [runner:open] Chapter 07 · Opening checklist — Opening checklist\nIf you open, this is your list. Do the job, then tap it.\n### Tick, then Submit\n- Opening: The bar and the count show how far along you are.\n- Do the job. Then tap it.: Each tick saves right away. (Why: Only tick what you really did. Your initials go on this list.)\n- Work down the sections: Building, control rooms, kitchen, and on. Top to bottom.\n- Raise a flag: Unusual things only: broken, missing, damaged, unsafe. Say what and where. Add photos. (Why: It becomes a flag the office has to act on. How the shift went goes in Notes, not here.)\n- Your initials: Already filled in. Check they are yours.\n- Save = not finished yet: Takes you back to your studio page without submitting. Your ticks are kept. Come back and finish.\n- Submit opening: List done? Tap it. Ticks alone are not enough. (Why: No Submit = tomorrow the office sees a red “never submitted” on this studio.)\n- Could not finish something?: Submit anyway. Say what and why in Raise a flag. (Why: Submitted with a problem always beats never submitted.)\n- Done: Submit takes you back to your studio page. Open the list again and it says Submitted.\n\n## [runner:close] Chapter 08 · Closing checklist — Closing checklist\nIf you close, this is the last thing you do in the building.\n### The last list of the night\n- Closing: Same as opening. Do it, tap it. Each tick saves. (Why: Closing at 2 AM Friday still belongs to Thursday. The app knows.)\n- Count first, tick second: These two are counts. Tick them only after you counted. (Why: A tick says “I counted”. The petty cash count itself goes in Petty cash. Chapter 09.)\n- The last walk: Opener’s start time, doors, tenants out, alarm, front door, gate. Tick each one as you do it. (Why: A door left unlocked all night is the worst thing a closer can leave behind.)\n- Raise a flag: Same as opening. Unusual things only.\n- Submit closing: The last tap before you walk out. (Why: No Submit = a red “never submitted” in the morning.)\n- Before you close: A session today has not been submitted. The app shows you which one. (Why: Closing is the last moment you are still in the building. It is your last chance to turn it in.)\n- Yours? Tap Submit on that row.: It opens that work order. Submit it. Then come back and close.\n- Not yours?: Session still running, or another runner’s? Tap Not mine — close. (Why: It asks. It does not trap you. The office still sees the open session in the morning, with a name on it.)\n\n## [runner:cash] Chapter 09 · Petty cash — Petty cash\nThe cash box. Write down every dollar in or out. Count the box at close.\n### Log it, count it, close it\n- Opening: What the box should start with: the last count, plus or minus anything logged since. You cannot change it. (Why: Tonight starts where the last count ended. That is how every dollar is tracked.)\n- Box does not match Opening?: Tap Opening to see where the number came from. Do not try to fix it. Count the box and type it into Counted at close. (Why: The difference goes to the office. They would rather know.)\n- Money moved? Tap + Add: Every time cash leaves the box or goes in. (Why: If it is not written down, the box is just “short” and nobody knows why.)\n- What, and how much: Type what it was for. Type the amount.\n- Out or In: It starts on Out: you spent it. Tap it to flip to In: money put into the box. (Why: Almost everything is Out. In is only when someone physically puts money in the box.)\n- The math: Opening + in − out = what should be in the box.\n- Counted at close: Count the real cash. Type the number. It is never filled in for you. (Why: Counting is the whole point. A copied number is not a count.)\n- Green = it matches: The box and the math agree.\n- Short?: Count again. Still short? Type the real number anyway. (Why: That is fine to record. The office would rather know than find out later.)\n- Tap Save: Nothing on this page reaches the office until you do.\n- Closing out: One last look at the numbers.\n- If it is short: It says by how much. Add a note: what you think happened.\n- Tomorrow’s opening: Your count is where tomorrow starts. (Why: Your name goes on this count.)\n- Close out the night: Tap it. Now it is saved.\n- Nothing moved tonight?: Still count the box and type the number in Counted at close. Then tap Counted — no change, and Close out the night. (Why: A quiet night still needs a count. With the box left empty it is recorded as “not counted”.)\n- It asks: “Is this really money going into the box?”: You typed the box total as Cash in. Tap That’s not right. (Why: Cash in is only NEW money put into the box. What was already there is the Opening.)\n- It asks: “This was already recorded”: Money moved again? Tap Add a new entry. Change a saved row only if it was typed wrong. (Why: The office can already see that row. Two entries keep both on the record.)\n- Previous days: The last 14 days. Read only.\n\n## [runner:stock] Chapter 10 · Stock list — Stock list\nCount what is on the shelves. Mark what is running out. That is how it gets bought.\n### Count, mark, save\n- Paramount has two lists: PRS Stock: every night. Office: Wednesdays only.\n- The count at the top: How many items you have counted, and how many are low.\n- Tap a shelf to open it: Fridge, Kitchen, Lounge and so on. Go stand there and count. (Why: It is grouped by place so you count one spot at a time.)\n- Last count: The small number is the last count and its date. (Why: It tells you what is normal. 6 yesterday and 0 today? Count again.)\n- Type how many: Count it. Type the number in Qty.\n- OK or LOW: Running out? Tap OK to flip it to LOW. (Why: LOW is how the office sees what is running out.)\n- Marked LOW: Orange = low. Tap it again to go back to OK.\n- Tap an item’s name to open it: A Notes box, and its last few counts underneath. (Why: A few words help the office: “Half a carton left.”)\n- LOW since…: Dashed = it was low last time. Still low? Tap it once. Restocked? Tap it twice. (Why: Dashed means nobody has checked it tonight.)\n- General notes: Anything about the whole list. This one box saves by itself.\n- Item not on the list?: Tap Missing an item? Tell the office.\n- Save stock list: The office gets nothing until you tap this. (Why: Your typing is kept on this phone, but kept is not sent.)\n- Done: It says Submitted.\n\n## [runner:notes] Chapter 11 · Notes — Notes\nOne message board per studio, plus General for everyone. Read it when you arrive. Write your handoff before you leave.\n### Read, then write\n- Everyone here sees this: Every runner at this studio. And the office.\n- Studio or General: PRS = this studio only. General = every studio. (Why: Handoffs go in the studio tab. They are filed with this studio’s night.)\n- Read first: The last runner’s handoff is here. Read it when you walk in. (Why: It is how you find out what is already going on.)\n- New since you looked: Everything under the orange line is new.\n- Orange bar = it is for you: Someone tagged you.\n- A task for you: A tag plus a time. You tick it on your studio page, under From the office. Not here.\n- Opener, Floater or Closer: Tap what you are tonight before you post. (Why: So the next person knows which shift wrote it.)\n- Type your note: Short and plain. What happened, and where.\n- Add a photo: Tap 📷. Up to 4. (Why: A photo beats a paragraph.)\n- Tag someone: Tap @ and pick a name. (Why: A tag points the note at one person. They see “for you”.)\n- Tag + time = a task: Tag one person and type a time, like 9am. It becomes a task for them. (Why: It lands on their studio page with a tick box. Studio tab only, not General.)\n- Send: Tap it. Posted.\n- Fix your own note: Tap ✎ on a note you wrote. You cannot delete a note. (Why: Notes are a record. Write them like one.)\n\n## [runner:memos] Chapter 12 · Memos — Memos\nMessages from management that you have to read.\n### Read it, sign it\n- Your memos: Every memo you have been sent. Each one says where it stands on the right. (Why: Memos are how the office tells you something that matters.)\n- Unread: Tap it to open it. A new memo also pops up by itself when you open your studio page.\n- Read it. All of it.: It is short on purpose.\n- I’ve read this: Check the initials are yours.\n- Sign & continue: Tap it. Done. (Why: Your initials say “I read this and I know it.”)\n- I’ll read it later: Really cannot right now? On the pop-up, this puts it off. It comes back the next time you open the app. (Why: Putting it off starts a 48-hour clock.)\n- Sign by…: You put it off. The list shows the day it must be signed by.\n- Needs your signature: The 48 hours are up. The app will not let you go on until you sign.\n- Signed: Done. It stays in the list so you can read it again.\n- Read: Some memos only need reading. No signature: you tap Got it.\n\n## [runner:punch] Chapter 13 · Missed a punch — Missed a punch\nForgot to clock in, clock out, or punch a meal? Report it the same day. It takes 30 seconds.\n### Thirty seconds\n- Check the name: It files under the name shown. Not you? Sign out first. (Why: It goes straight to the manager queue under that name.)\n- Which shift: The day the punch belongs to. After midnight, your shift started yesterday: tap Yesterday. (Why: This page goes by the calendar. At 1 AM, “Tonight” means the new day.)\n- What was missed: Clock in, Clock out, Meal out or Meal in.\n- The time it should say: Type it like 6:00 PM. With the colon. Always with AM or PM. (Why: Leave off AM or PM and “6:00” is read as 6 in the morning.)\n- Red message?: The app could not read the time. Type it like 6:00 PM.\n- Note: Optional. One line on why.\n- Submit: Tap Submit as your name. (Why: Same-day reports are the good kind. Report it the night it happens.)\n- Sent: It is in the manager queue.\n- Your last 90 days: Clean, 1 miss, 2 misses. Three or more shows in red. (Why: Reporting a miss is right. Not missing is better: clock in before anything else.)\n\n## [runner:rules] Chapter 14 · The rules — The rules\nIf you remember nothing else, remember these.\n### Nine rules\nYour PIN, your name. Never work under someone else’s sign-in. Pick the studio you are standing in. On a work order, nothing is saved until Save or Submit. ← and Cancel lose it. Ran over? Change End. Left early? Leave it. Always fill in Arrived and Left. Or No show. COD: signature, the right number, Save. Submit every session before you leave. Late beats never. Something wrong? Write it in Needs Attention, or Raise a flag. Everything else goes in Notes. Count the box. Type the real number. Even when it is short.\n### If something goes wrong\n- I submitted with a mistake: Open the work order. Fix it. Tap Update submission. No penalty.\n- I forgot to submit last night: It is on top of your studio page until the next morning. Open it, fill in Arrived and Left, submit. Already gone? Tell the office in Notes.\n- The day I need is locked: The office approved it. Tell the office in Notes.\n- The cash box is short: Count again. Type the real number. Add a note.\n- The app asked for my PIN again: Normal. It signs you out after 4 hours, and at 8:50 AM.\n- The app is doing something weird: First screen → Report a bug or an idea.\n- I do not know what to do: Ask the office in Notes. Tag them with @."
